window.PULSE_CURRENT = {"asOf":"2026-11-28T04:30:00Z","calendar":[{"date":"2026-11-26","event":"Printed: MOFCOM press conference (He Yadong): firmly opposes the Section 301 overcapacity tariff, reserves the right to take necessary measures, asks the US to implement the $30B reciprocal tariff cut; PBoC CNY 571.5B overnight against CNY 617B maturing (−CNY 45.5B); 10-year CGB 1.59%; onshore yuan 6.6600 (+136 pips); US markets closed","why":"Opposition without a named countermeasure; month-end money rolled off with funding flat"},{"date":"2026-11-27","event":"Printed: October industrial profits +20.1% y/y (January to October +16.0%, margin 5.69%); PBoC CNY 794B overnight (+CNY 222.5B net); fix 6.7075 (+21 pips); US early close 13:00 ET","why":"Profits confirm the upstream and chip economy is growing while autos, construction and steel lose money"},{"date":"2026-11-27","event":"Printed: State Council executive meeting readout at midday (national team named, Central Huijin quasi-stabilisation fund, sufficient liquidity, dividends and buybacks, long-term money, imported-risk defences); CSRC Wu Qing pledges incremental policies; PBoC Financial Stability Report 2026; PBoC CNY 794B overnight (net +CNY 222.5B); CSI 300 +4.17% to 4,063.06 on CNY 2,017.3B turnover; 10-year CGB 1.584%; yuan 6.6544","why":"The policy floor moved from the exchanges to the State Council and the CSI 300 closed back above the October low in one session; follow-through and the PMIs decide the posture."},{"date":"2026-11-27","event":"Printed: US half session Dow +1.18%, S&P 500 +1.60%, Nasdaq +2.31% (week +6.7%), semiconductor index about +5%; LME copper +3.29% to $12,262 after +6.4% intraday; Caixin on Vanke's three-year deferral terms and −48.2% sales","why":"The AI-hardware bid and the metals bounce returned together; developer credit did not join."},{"date":"2026-11-28","event":"MOFCOM suspension of the dual-use export ban to the US (gallium, germanium, antimony, superhard materials; stricter graphite review) takes effect, running to 27 Jan 2027","why":"Keeps the critical-minerals channel open past the 10 Jan truce date; any US reciprocal step on chips or tariffs is the thing to watch"},{"date":"2026-11-30","event":"November NBS PMIs","why":"Manufacturing prior 49.3, new orders 49.4, non-manufacturing 49.7, construction 48.0; new orders back above 50 would reopen the Recovery case, manufacturing below 49 would raise the Contraction question."},{"date":"2026-11-30","event":"Margin-financing minimum ratio cut from 100% to 80% takes effect on the Shanghai, Shenzhen and Beijing exchanges (same day as the NBS PMIs)","why":"Xinhua cites a theoretical CNY 400B of incremental money; whether margin balances turn up from CNY 2,134.81B (23 Nov, −CNY 8.99B on the day) is the test of the 22 Nov package"},{"date":"2026-12-01","event":"NDRC outbound investment management measures take effect","why":"Adds reporting of significant adverse developments and overseas reinvestment for Chinese outbound investors"},{"date":"2026-12-01","event":"November RatingDog manufacturing PMI","why":"Prior 52.0; whether the exporter survey holds above 51 while the official index sits at 49.3 and export delivery value grows 18.6%"},{"date":"2026-12-01","event":"EU temporary safeguard measures on hybrid vehicles (preliminary finding of 24 Nov)","why":"MOFCOM reserved WTO dispute settlement and trade compensation; exports to the EU rose 24.4% y/y in October with autos the fastest-growing line"},{"date":"2026-12-03","event":"November RatingDog services PMI","why":"Prior 50.8; a print below 50 would put the private services survey in contraction for the first time in nearly four years, with the services production index already slowing to 4.6%"},{"date":"2026-12-04","event":"Hang Seng index changes implemented after the close (effective 7 Dec)","why":"Hang Seng Tech widened from 30 to 50 stocks with Guangfa estimating about HK$29.1B of passive demand; HSCEI adds Zhipu and MiniMax"},{"date":"2026-12-07","event":"Hang Seng index changes take effect","why":"Hang Seng Index unchanged at 95; HSCEI adds Zhipu and MiniMax, drops PSBC and Shenzhou; Hang Seng Tech index 30 to 50 constituents (CATL, Luxshare, Victory Giant, Innolight, Montage, YOFC, Kingsoft Cloud, Biren and others), 8% cap"},{"date":"2026-12-08","event":"November trade","why":"Prior exports +35.2%, imports +41.6%; Dongfang Jincheng expects exports to stay above 20%; the first full month after the truce extension and the BIS remote-access rule"},{"date":"2026-12-08","event":"Vanke 22 Vanke MTN004 second holder meeting on extension terms (CNY 1.199B outstanding; record date 7 Dec, votes by 17:00 on 10 Dec, principal due 15 Dec)","why":"Vanke's first dated public extension vote after a year of implied extensions; the Huafa curve shows how the market prices a failed one"},{"date":"2026-12-09","event":"FOMC decision (US)","why":"A 25 bp hike is priced near 97% after the discount-rate minutes showed eight of twelve reserve banks asking for 4.25%; the US 10-year at 4.9038% is about 332 bp above the CGB; JPMorgan expects three hikes to 4.50% to 4.75%"},{"date":"2026-12-09","event":"November CPI and PPI","why":"Prior CPI 0.7%, PPI 5.7%; whether the m/m PPI slowdown and the oil and metals fall show in the y/y, and whether food stops falling with retail sales at 0.4%"},{"date":"2026-12-11","event":"CSI 300, SSE 50, SSE 180, SSE 380, STAR 50 and STAR 100 sample changes effective after the close (CSI 300 30 names; SSE 50 adds China Jushi, Baofeng Energy, YOFC, Piotech and Yuanjie; STAR 50 adds Yandong Micro, Hwatsing, Sijia Photons, Xi'an ESWIN and CXMT); Evergrande Auto last trading day","why":"Passive flows into the chip and optical names that led the 27 Nov rally; Shenzhen Component and ChiNext changes follow on 14 Dec."},{"date":"2026-12-12","event":"November credit (approximate; PBoC releases between the 10th and 15th)","why":"Prior TSF 7.2%, M2 7.1%, loans 4.7%; whether household loans turn positive after −CNY 430B in October"},{"date":"2026-12-14","event":"G20 summit in Miami (14 to 15 Dec); Xi and Trump reported to plan a fourth meeting this year","why":"The next chance for tariff, chip or purchase terms before the 10 Jan 2027 truce expiry; the 24 Nov minerals extension runs to 27 Jan"},{"date":"2026-12-14","event":"Evergrande Auto delisting takes effect at 09:00; Shenzhen Component, ChiNext, SZSE 100 and ChiNext 50 sample changes effective","why":"A delisting that closes the Evergrande equity chapter in Hong Kong while Vanke's extension is being voted."},{"date":"2026-12-15","event":"November activity data and 70-city prices (approximate; NBS mid-month)","why":"Prior industrial production 4.8%, retail sales 0.4%, FAI −8.1%, unemployment 5.1%, home prices −2.4%; Dongfang Jincheng expects industrial production near 5.0%, retail sales near 1.6% and property −22%; the December Politburo meeting and the Central Economic Work Conference usually fall in the same fortnight (dates not announced)"},{"date":"2026-12-15","event":"22 Vanke MTN004 maturity (CNY 1.199B) if the 8 Dec extension vote fails","why":"The first Vanke public bond with a dated outcome; Caixin says holders may prefer a declared default to a three-year deferral with a small upfront payment."},{"date":"2026-12-21","event":"December LPR fixing","why":"A 19th hold is the base case after Wang Qing's 2027 call; Dong Ximiao sees a small cut as possible after the Central Economic Work Conference"}],"cb":{"label":"Easing","note":"The 1-year LPR was held at 3.00% and the 5-year at 3.50% on 20 Nov, an 18th month unchanged since the 10 bp cut of May 2025. The PBoC lent CNY 794B overnight at 1.25% on 27 Nov against CNY 571.5B maturing, a CNY 222.5B net injection for the last session before the turn, after the CNY 45.5B net drain of 26 Nov and the CNY 321B injection of 25 Nov; the overnight repo fixing FDR001 rose 1.0 bp to 1.28% and FDR007 1.45 bp to 1.3745%, overnight Shibor rose 0.7 bp to 1.28%, 7-day Shibor 1.0 bp to 1.377% and 14-day 0.18 bp to 1.3998% with 1-month flat at 1.39%, and 1-year bank NCDs printed about 1.41% to 1.42% in primary. The active 10-year CGB (260016) closed at 1.584% at 16:30, down 0.9 bp, the 30-year at 2.04% (−1 bp) and the active CDB bond at 1.718% (−1.2 bp) after a late recovery, while the 30-year future fell 0.30% to 116.850 and the 10-year 0.03% to 109.915; bonds did not sell on the 4% equity day. The fix was set 21 pips stronger at 6.7075 on 27 Nov and the onshore yuan closed 56 pips stronger at 6.6544 at 16:30, with the night session at 6.6541 and the offshore rate at 6.6553 in late New York trading as the dollar index rose 0.24% to 104.03. The PBoC's Financial Stability Report 2026, published 27 Nov, says it is studying institutional arrangements to provide liquidity to non-bank institutions in specific scenarios and will use the two capital-market support tools, which is the monetary side of the State Council's 'sufficient liquidity' instruction. The stance stays Easing by instrument with the LPR on hold; the November MLF and outright-repo reductions are quantity choices at an unchanged price."},"cbName":"PBoC stance","conflicts":[{"a":"October industrial profits +20.1% y/y (January to October +16.0%, margin 5.69%, electronics profit doubled, nonferrous +71.7%, coal +61.4%, high-tech manufacturing +50.9%); October exports +35.2% y/y with integrated circuits +137.1%; export delivery value +18.6%; high-tech manufacturing output +17.6%; CAAM vehicle exports +60.2%; PPI +5.7%; RatingDog manufacturing 52.0, an 11th month above 50; TSF stock growth up to 7.2%; SAFE October bank FX settlement surplus $55.0B; January to October fiscal revenue +4.9% with securities stamp duty +54.1% and high-tech FDI +31.3%; NEA October power consumption +1.6% y/y","b":"October industrial production 4.8% (consensus 5.3%), retail sales 0.4% (consensus 0.8%) with autos −21.4%, FAI −8.1% year to date with property −21.6%, infrastructure −5.1% and manufacturing −2.9%, services production index 4.6%; NBS manufacturing PMI 49.3 with new orders 49.4, non-manufacturing 49.7 with construction 48.0; CPI 0.7% with food −2.9%; new yuan loans −CNY 100B with household loans −CNY 430B; consumer confidence 89.0; January to October profits in autos −26.0%, non-metallic minerals −46.7%, agricultural processing −19.5%, steel −14.2% and power −18.4%, foreign-invested profits +0.2%, receivables +10.5% with the collection period at 72.2 days; Xiaomi Q3 revenue −5.2%","read":"The exporter, upstream and AI-capex economy is growing profits at 20% while the domestic demand economy is flat to contracting and its industries are losing money; the framework reads leading over coincident, and both are below 50 or decelerating. Regime Slowdown. The 27 Nov equity rally does not resolve this: it was a State Council mandate on CNY 2T of turnover with bonds unmoved, and the 30 Nov PMIs are the next real-economy print.","trigger":"30 Nov NBS PMIs (new orders above 50 reopens Recovery; manufacturing below 49 raises Contraction); 1 Dec RatingDog; 8 Dec trade; mid-December activity data"},{"a":"PPI +5.7% y/y and purchase prices +7.9% with coal mining +36.6% and oil and gas extraction +35.0%; CICC: Qinhuangdao thermal coal CNY 1,019 a tonne, +24% y/y; US October PPI 6.5% y/y with FedWatch at about 94% for a December hike and JPMorgan expecting three hikes; TrendForce: DRAM contract prices +10% to 15% in Q4; Alibaba: 2027 and 2028 the tightest compute years","b":"PPI m/m slowed to 0.7% from 1.2%; CPI 0.7% with food −2.9%, core 0.8% and services 0.7%; retail sales 0.4% and consumer confidence 89.0; LME copper $11,850 on 26 Nov (+1.72%) after the 25 Nov settlement fell to $11,703, an 11-month low 18% below 9 Nov; iron ore $90.64 with the Dalian contract −2.27% in the night session; the active 10-year CGB at 1.59% and the LPR held with no cut expected before 2027; the US 10-year 4.862% after core PCE 3.3%; industrial costs down 0.42 yuan per 100 yuan of revenue","read":"The producer-price pulse is cost-push from coal, oil and chips, not domestic demand; the metals break of 17 to 24 Nov and Goldman's memory-price cut say the cost side is rolling over while oil is back above $80 on Hormuz and the consumer side has not moved; the bond market prices neither inflation nor a cut, and US core PCE at 3.3% keeps the Fed hike that limits the PBoC. Inflation score stays at 48. LME copper bounced 3.29% to $12,262 on 27 Nov, still 13% below the 9 Nov settlement, so November PPI inherits a lower metals base than October while Brent at $95 keeps the oil leg.","trigger":"9 Dec CPI and PPI (whether the m/m slowdown and the oil and metals fall show in the y/y); the 9 Dec FOMC"},{"a":"Truce dated to 10 Jan 2027; Xi and Trump agreed on 19 Nov to draft an action plan on a constructive relationship of strategic stability and are reported to plan a G20 meeting in Miami on 14 to 15 Dec; MOFCOM on 24 Nov extended the suspension of the gallium, germanium, antimony and superhard-material export ban to the US to 27 Jan 2027; the China-US agricultural working group held its first meeting in Beijing on 23 and 24 Nov, which MOFCOM called candid and constructive; the USTR proposal exempts about $30B of Chinese imports under the Board of Trade review, takes effect no earlier than a 25 Jan 2027 hearing and, Greer says, maintains the deals made; a senior US official expects no Chinese retaliation and Guo Jiakun threatened none; the October US surplus about $33B with exports to the US +32.9%; MOFCOM's He Yadong on 26 Nov reserved the right to take necessary measures without naming one and asked Washington to implement the $30B reciprocal tariff cut, with both teams in close communication on extending the Kuala Lumpur arrangement","b":"USTR proposed on 25 Nov a 20% Section 301 overcapacity tariff on China on top of the roughly 25% first-term duties, rising to 40% if the truce unravels, alongside 10% to 20% on 13 other partners; Guo Jiakun called overcapacity a false issue used for political manipulation; Trump wants 'only older chips' to go to China; the BIS remote-access rule of 16 Nov stands and Commerce added Alibaba's Apex Enterprise Solutions to the entity list; Nvidia's Q4 guide excludes China and its shares fell 3.91% on 25 Nov after 5.86% on 24 Nov; the EU's hybrid-vehicle safeguard runs from 1 Dec with a 86,301-unit China quota for December to February; Alibaba says models will train on domestic chips","read":"Beijing extended the minerals pause two months past the truce date and held the agriculture talks while Washington put a 20% to 40% tariff on the table for late January and Brussels' auto channel tightened from 1 Dec; the trade channel stays open under a truce dated to 10 Jan 2027, and that date now decides whether the new tariff is 20% or 40%. The State Council's 'imported risk' line on 27 Nov is the domestic hedge against the 301 outcome.","trigger":"The Federal Register notice with product lists and comment deadlines; the 1 Dec EU safeguard; 8 Dec trade data; 14 to 15 Dec G20 Miami; 10 Jan 2027 truce expiry; 25 Jan 2027 USTR hearing; 27 Jan 2027 end of the minerals suspension"},{"a":"Home prices −2.4% y/y in October after −2.8%, the smallest fall since November 2025, and −0.1% m/m; Shanghai +2.7% with tier-one resale prices up an eighth month; second-hand transactions +11.4% year to date; new mortgage rates about 3.1%; unemployment 5.1%; the 5-year LPR at 3.50% with Dong Ximiao seeing a possible cut around year-end","b":"Property investment −21.6% year to date (Western Securities: October alone −33.2%), new-home sales −13.7% by area and −14.3% by value, cement output −1.3%; household loans −CNY 430B in October with medium and long-term loans falling; CAAM domestic vehicle sales −26.6%; construction PMI 48.0 with construction new orders 40.0; iron ore $90.64 and LME copper $11,882; 25 Huafa 04 fell 31% on 20 Nov after 22 Huafa 03 fell 25% on 19 Nov; 23 Huazong 03 −26.41%; R&F's H16 R&F 5 holders approved a grace period while the restructuring proposal failed; 22 Huafa Industrial MTN001A fell 43.31% on 23 Nov; Vanke is reported to be asking holders of the 22 Vanke MTN004 (CNY 1.2B, due 15 Dec, vote 8 Dec) for a three-year principal deferral with an early cash payment below half of January's 40%, after a nine-month net loss of CNY 8.99B and contract sales −48.3%; steel profits −14.2% and non-metallic mineral profits −46.7% for January to October; NAFMII censured Tianjin Real Estate Group; Jinke, Risesun and CFLD traded below CNY 1; Caixin (27 Nov): Vanke's January to September sales −48.2% to CNY 52B with operating cash outflow of CNY 2.2B and cash of CNY 52.5B, a three-year deferral sought on the CNY 1.2B MTN004 due 15 Dec with an upfront payment 'well below' 40%, and exchange-traded Huafa and Huazong bonds down 16% to 20% on 27 Nov","read":"Prices are stabilising in the tier-one resale market while volumes, investment and developer credit keep falling and the Huafa curve is still repricing bond by bond; the property cycle is the drag on local finances, household wealth and commodity demand. Signal warn on prices, bad on investment. The 27 Nov State Council measures are equity liquidity and do not reach developer credit; iron ore stayed at $90.69 while copper rose 3.29%.","trigger":"Mid-December 70-city prices and property investment; Vanke's holder briefings from 27 Nov and the 8 Dec MTN004 vote (ballots by 10 Dec, principal due 15 Dec); Huafa extension outcomes; R&F's next step after the failed proposal; the December Politburo meeting and Central Economic Work Conference"},{"a":"Policy floor written into the institutions: the State Council readout of 27 Nov names the national team, assigns Central Huijin a quasi-stabilisation-fund function and promises sufficient liquidity, the CSRC pledges incremental policies the same evening, the PBoC studies liquidity for non-banks, the margin-financing minimum falls to 80% on 30 Nov, equity-ETF subscriptions exceed CNY 800B since October, buyback re-loan contracts about CNY 630B this week; the CSI 300 rose 4.17% to 4,063.06 on three-exchange turnover of CNY 2,017.3B with 5,382 up against 181 down and 426 limit-ups, back above the October low, the ChiNext +11.61%, the STAR 50 +15.07%, the Hang Seng +2.11% with the tech index +6.45%, southbound buying back above HK$4B, LME copper +3.29%","b":"A one-session move with the 10-year CGB at 1.584% (−0.9 bp) and the yuan 56 pips firmer, so bonds and FX saw no regime change; the leaders were the AI-hardware and chip names that fell hardest and the only prior bid (banks, coal, high-dividend) fell; Yu Fenghui calls it an oversold, sentiment-driven repair rather than a fundamental reversal, the comparable days (30 Sep and 8 Oct 2024) were followed by retracements, the CSI 300 is still 3.7% below the 4,217.68 reversal line and the November PMIs print on 30 Nov with new orders at 49.4; no national-team purchase amount for 27 Nov was disclosed","read":"The framework reads leading data first and the leading set is still below 50, so the rally is treated as a policy floor that raises the markets reading (22 to 30) without touching the regime; the posture stays Risk-off until a second close above 3,958.14 with positive breadth (Neutral) or a close above 4,217.68 on CNY 2T turnover (Risk-on).","trigger":"30 Nov: CSI 300 close against 3,958.14 and breadth on the day the margin cut takes effect and the NBS PMIs print; any disclosed Central Huijin or national-team purchase; the CSRC's incremental measures; a 10-year CGB move out of 1.55% to 1.60%."}],"drivers":[{"date":"2026-11-27","impact":"The explicit mandate turned a 0.24% midday gain into a 4.17% close for the CSI 300 on CNY 2T of turnover; Chen Guo (Eastmoney Securities) calls 'national team plus sufficient liquidity' a strong policy floor, Guo Lei (Guangfa) says institutionalised stabilisation lowers the tail-risk premium, Yu Fenghui calls it an oversold repair rather than a fundamental reversal.","src":"Xinhua readout via 21st Century Business Herald, Time Weekly via Sohu, Sina hourly reports and Zhitong via Longbridge","tag":"Policy","title":"State Council executive meeting (Li Qiang) issues a midday readout on deepening capital-market investment and financing reform: the capital market 'bears on the overall economic situation'; keep improving the stabilisation mechanism, implement existing policies and plan incremental ones; push dividends and buybacks; 'step up the market-stabilising role of the national team' (first use of the term in a State Council readout) and optimise Central Huijin's quasi-stabilisation-fund function; 'provide sufficient liquidity support'; improve the entry policies for insurance, enterprise-annuity and social-security money; strengthen defences against imported risk; accelerate the multi-tier market; punish financial fraud and illegal share reductions. Second capital-market readout in a month after 6 Nov.","url":"https://www.21jingji.com/article/20261127/herald/a821555019a1c5918a4ff80b6c73c4ed.html"},{"date":"2026-11-27","impact":"The first reversal condition (a close above 3,958.14 with advancers outnumbering decliners) is met in one session; the 4,217.68 line is 3.7% away. Posture stays Risk-off pending a second close; the markets score rises to 30.","src":"FX168 flash; Tencent daily klines; 21st Century Business Herald; Sina hourly reports; Tencent News; Sina close report","tag":"Markets","title":"27 Nov close: CSI 300 +4.17% to 4,063.06 (+162.51; open 3,909.08, high 4,067.01, low 3,883.80), first close above the 23 Oct low since 19 Nov; Shanghai Composite +3.73% to 3,606.49 (open 3,482.38, high 3,610.72, low 3,467.41); Shenzhen Component +7.24% to 10,814.02; ChiNext +11.61% to 2,443.96 (largest since 8 Oct 2024); STAR 50 +15.07% to 1,346.25; STAR composite +14.21%; BSE 50 about +13%. Three-exchange turnover CNY 2,017.3B (+CNY 691.3B, fifth-largest daily increase on record, first CNY 2T day in 16 sessions); 5,382 up, 181 down, 426 limit-ups (most since 8 Oct 2024), no limit-downs; semiconductors +15.29%, electronic chemicals +14.74%, software +11.46%; banks, coal and high-dividend names down; main funds net +CNY 104.9B to 107.7B, electronics +CNY 73.6B; E Fund ChiNext ETF CNY 22.09B, Huaxia STAR 50 ETF CNY 18.63B, China-Korea semiconductor ETF a record CNY 31.7B; week: Shanghai +2.06%, Shenzhen +5.44%, ChiNext +10.48%.","url":"https://www.fx168news.com/express/fastnews/1476363"},{"date":"2026-11-27","impact":"The AI names that led the November fall led the bounce and the mainland bid returned; the index is within 0.6% of the 19 Nov close with the 7 Dec tech-index widening ahead.","src":"FX168 flash; Tencent hkHSI kline; China News Service via Sohu; 21st Century Business Herald; Sina; Securities Times via Sohu; Zhitong via Longbridge","tag":"Markets","title":"Hong Kong 27 Nov: Hang Seng +2.11% to 22,694.77 (+467.89; open and low 22,263.70, high 22,781.03, turnover HK$257.14B); tech index +6.45% to 3,637.88; HSCEI +2.01% to 7,644.18; red chips +1.23% to 3,761.25; week +1.27%, +3.61%, +1.19%. Hua Hong +20.69%, SMIC +16.39%, Biren +25.4%, Iluvatar +26.3%, Zhipu +18.57%, MiniMax +17.19%, Lenovo +8.99%, SenseTime +9.05%, Meituan +8.21% after Q3 revenue CNY 115.56B (+21.6%), Alibaba +7.03%, Kuaishou +6.83%, JD +5.36%, Xiaomi +4.51%, Tencent +3.23%, Lingbao Gold +10%. Southbound net buying above HK$4B at 15:19 after the HK$21.35B sale of 26 Nov (morning active list: Shenhua +HK$1.11B, SMIC +HK$900M via Shenzhen Connect, Alibaba +HK$1.27B across both). Evergrande Auto to be delisted 14 Dec; Nikkei +2.11% to 58,711.11, Kospi +4.34% to 4,915.68.","url":"https://www.fx168news.com/express/fastnews/1476398"},{"date":"2026-11-27","impact":"The regulator and the central bank both frame 'sufficient liquidity' as capital-market tools at an unchanged policy rate; bonds and the yuan barely moved on the equity day.","src":"Securities Times and Shanghai Securities News via 21st Century Business Herald (CSRC); 21st Century Business Herald morning news (PBoC report, CD rules); 24TopNews bond daily; FX168; Sing Tao","tag":"Policy","title":"CSRC chairman Wu Qing convenes an enlarged Party committee on the State Council meeting and commits to 'implement existing policies in detail and, with relevant parties, promptly study and issue incremental policies', with five tasks: the stabilisation mechanism (national team, Central Huijin, the two structural monetary tools, dividends and buybacks), medium- and long-term money, imported-risk defences, reform and full-chain supervision. PBoC Financial Stability Report 2026 (27 Nov): studying institutional arrangements to provide liquidity to non-bank institutions in specific scenarios; use of the two capital-market tools. PBoC 27 Nov: CNY 794B overnight at 1.25% against CNY 571.5B maturing (net +CNY 222.5B); FDR001 1.28% (+1.0 bp), FDR007 1.3745%, overnight Shibor 1.28%, 7-day 1.377%; active 10-year CGB 1.584% (−0.9 bp), 30-year 2.04%, 10-year CDB 1.718%; TL −0.30%, T −0.03%; fix 6.7075 (+21 pips), onshore close 6.6544 (+56 pips), night 6.6541, offshore 6.6553; new large-denomination CD rules effective 21 Mar 2027 and revised deposit and loan rate rules.","url":"https://www.21jingji.com/article/20261128/herald/4a067a63815a98c47fc02cd67651bb03.html"},{"date":"2026-11-27","impact":"Developer credit did not join the equity rally; a rejected or diluted extension on 8 Dec would be the first dated Vanke event with a public outcome.","src":"Caixin Global; 24TopNews bond daily","tag":"Property","title":"Caixin: Vanke proposes a three-year deferral on the CNY 1.2B 22 Vanke MTN004 due 15 Dec with an upfront cash payment 'well below' the 40% agreed in the first extension; underwriters to brief holders from 27 Nov ahead of the 8 Dec vote; January to September contract sales −48.2% to CNY 52B, operating cash outflow CNY 2.2B, cash CNY 52.5B at end-September (−CNY 6.6B from June); Shenzhen Metro provided about CNY 4.5B for the upfront payments on ten extended bonds; Vanke plans bond-by-bond talks rather than a comprehensive restructuring. Exchange-traded property bonds on 27 Nov: 20 Huafa −20%, 24 Huazong 01 −16%, 25 Zhuhua Y3 +34%.","url":"https://www.caixinglobal.com/2026-11-27/vanke-seeks-second-extension-on-12-billion-yuan-bond-102509069.html"},{"date":"2026-11-27","impact":"The AI-hardware bid returned on both sides of the Pacific and copper had its best day since February on the Chinese stabilisation signal; oil fell back below $96 Brent while gold rebounded more than $100.","src":"21st Century Business Herald morning news; Sina international finance roundup of 28 Nov; Sing Tao metals wire; Wallstreetcn via 163 and Longbridge; Trading Economics","tag":"Markets","title":"Overseas 27 Nov: US half session Dow +1.18% to 50,774.94 (week +5.5%), S&P 500 +1.60% to 7,297.49 (+5.6%), Nasdaq +2.31% to 24,129.50 (+6.7%), Philadelphia semiconductor index about +5% (+9% on the week) with SanDisk +16%, Micron and SK Hynix +7%, Coherent +14%; US 10-year 4.928%, 5-year 4.746%, 30-year 5.325%; dollar index 104.03 (+0.24%); COMEX gold +2.94% to $3,639.60 (spot $3,665.02), silver +7.76% to $43.167; WTI −0.72% to $83.08, Brent −1.17% to $95.44; DAX +2.14% to 25,231.42, CAC +1.61%, FTSE +1.75%. LME copper +3.29% to $12,262 (intraday +6.4% to $12,595, largest since February; 3-month $12,251), week +0.84% after three falls; tin +8.65% to $41,170, zinc +1.68%, nickel +0.44%, aluminium −0.77%, lead −0.80%; SHFE copper +5.5%, COMEX copper +3.38% to $5.517; monitored stocks about 1.105M t; iron ore $90.69 (+0.06%).","url":"https://m.21jingji.com/article/20261128/herald/9b9bb11d97ae9943bb4f4fa1c69a9c26.html"},{"date":"2026-11-27","impact":"A profit recovery at Meituan after the subsidy war and record dividends and buybacks give the State Council's dividend-and-buyback line something to point at.","src":"China News Service via Sohu; 21st Century Business Herald morning news; Sina hourly reports; Zhitong via Longbridge","tag":"Earnings","title":"Meituan Q3 2026: revenue CNY 115.56B (+21.6% y/y), core local commerce revenue CNY 78.28B, adjusted net profit CNY 1.85B; shares +8.21% in Hong Kong. Kweichow Moutai announces a 2026 interim dividend of CNY 25.60 a share (CNY 32.0B in total). Ganfeng Lithium makes its first A-share buyback (CNY 9.81M); Will Semiconductor's chairman proposes a CNY 500M to 1B buyback and Goke Microelectronics CNY 250M to 500M. SASAC's Li Zhen tells central SOEs to merge overlapping and low-price-competition businesses; SAMR summons 15 e-bike makers. CSI 300 and SSE 50 sample changes effective after the 11 Dec close (30 CSI 300 names; SSE 50 adds China Jushi, Baofeng Energy, YOFC, Piotech and Yuanjie), Shenzhen indexes on 14 Dec.","url":"https://www.sohu.com/a/1107353939_122014422"},{"date":"2026-11-27","impact":"Argues against Contraction without changing Slowdown: the profit is prices, exports and AI hardware while the domestic-demand chains lose money","src":"NBS via Sina (Cailianshe), Guangming Daily and The Paper","tag":"Data","title":"October industrial profits +20.1% y/y, 5.7 points faster than September; January to October +16.0% to CNY 6,737.4B (revenue +6.7%, margin 5.69% +0.45 pt, costs 85.06 per 100 yuan −0.42): electronics profit doubled (9.7 points of the growth), nonferrous +71.7%, coal +61.4%, chemicals +50.3%, high-tech manufacturing +50.9%, refining back in profit; autos −26.0%, non-metallic minerals −46.7%, agricultural processing −19.5%, steel −14.2%, power −18.4%; state +13.0%, private +11.4%, foreign-invested +0.2%; receivables +10.5% (72.2 days), finished-goods inventory +12.0%, asset-liability ratio 58.6%","url":"https://finance.sina.cn/2026-11-27/detail-inkacqyr3341919.d.html"},{"date":"2026-11-27","impact":"The overnight tool carries the month-end turn at an unchanged price","src":"China News Service; 10jqka bond midday","tag":"Policy","title":"PBoC lends CNY 794B overnight at 1.25% on 27 Nov against CNY 571.5B maturing, a CNY 222.5B net injection for the last session of November; overnight Shibor 1.28% (+0.7 bp), 7-day 1.377% (+1.0 bp), FR007 1.43% at midday; 27 Nov fix 6.7075 (+21 pips)","url":"https://www.chinanews.com.cn/cj/2026/11-27/10738525.shtml"},{"date":"2026-11-26","impact":"A pause on shrinking volume after the new low, lifted by banks and oil in the last hour; posture Risk-off","src":"Jinrong Jie via Sohu; Tencent klines; The Paper; Sina hourly report","tag":"Markets","title":"26 Nov close: CSI 300 +0.06% to 3,900.55 (+2.31; open 3,918.02, high 3,922.29, low 3,877.82), 57.59 points below the 23 Oct low; Shanghai Composite +0.01% to 3,476.88 (open 3,490.14, high 3,497.81, low 3,455.04); Shenzhen Component −0.02%, ChiNext +0.29% to 2,189.82, STAR 50 −1.36% to 1,169.99, CSI 500 −0.46%, CSI 1000 −0.18%, BSE 50 −0.45%; turnover CNY 1,317.3B (−CNY 65.8B), the lowest of the month; 1,766 up, 3,642 down, 68 limit-ups, 8 limit-downs; precious metals +3.65%, oil and gas extraction +3.30%, components +3.22%, coal +2.26%, airlines −3.58%, biologics −2.47%; Nanjing Bank and CITIC Bank record highs intraday","url":"https://www.sohu.com/a/1106771945_114984"},{"date":"2026-11-26","impact":"The bounce came as the mainland bid reversed into a record ETF sale","src":"FX168; Korea Finance Daily (Chinese); 21st Century Business Herald; Tencent hkHSI kline","tag":"Markets","title":"Hong Kong 26 Nov: Hang Seng +1.19% to 22,226.88 (+260.87; open 22,234.89, midday 22,373.81, morning high 22,543.75), back above 22,000 after seven falls; tech index +1.16% to 3,417.38 after 11 falls; HSCEI +1.47% to 7,493.34; red chips +1.14%; southbound net sale HK$21.35B, the largest since 9 Apr (Tracker Fund HK$8.45B, HSCEI ETF HK$2.19B, Southern HSTECH ETF HK$1.83B, Zhipu HK$943M, Hua Hong HK$501M, Meituan HK$489M; Tencent bought HK$147M); Zhipu +8.12%, MiniMax +7.49%, Zijin Gold International +5.69%, PetroChina +4.38%, Sunmi −31.75%, airlines −4.5% to −5.3%; Goldman 2027: Hong Kong overweight, A-shares equal-weight, earnings +15%, MSCI China 9.5x","url":"https://news.jkn.co.kr/editions/chinese/post/1127074"},{"date":"2026-11-26","impact":"Month-end money rolled off with funding flat; the curve prices supply, not a cut","src":"Zheshang Bank FICC via Sohu; CFETS via 10jqka; Sina citing CITIC fixed income; FX168; NBD via Sohu","tag":"Policy","title":"PBoC on 26 Nov: CNY 571.5B overnight reverse repo at 1.25% against CNY 617B maturing, a CNY 45.5B net drain after the CNY 321B injection of 25 Nov; DR001 1.27% (flat), DR007 1.37% (−1 bp), overnight Shibor 1.273%; active 10-year CGB 1.59% (+0.1 bp; CITIC 1.593%, +0.4 bp, after touching 1.60%), 30-year 2.049% (+0.85 bp), CDB 1.728% (+1.65 bp), CGB-CDB spread about 15 bp; cash bonds CNY 1.65T (−5.88%); 46 NCDs CNY 84.8B; fix 6.7096 (−8 pips), onshore close 6.6600 (+136 pips), night session 6.6609","url":"https://www.sohu.com/a/1106952831_122014422"},{"date":"2026-11-26","impact":"Opposition without a named countermeasure keeps the truce and the $30B track intact to 10 Jan 2027","src":"Xinhua via Sohu; CCTV via The Paper","tag":"Trade","title":"MOFCOM spokesman He Yadong: the Section 301 overcapacity investigation is typical unilateralism that violates WTO rules, China firmly opposes it, will follow developments closely, reserves the right to take necessary measures and will defend its legitimate rights; the proposal exempts the products on the $30B reciprocal tariff-reduction list, and Beijing wants Washington to speed its internal procedures and implement it; the two trade teams are in close communication on extending the Kuala Lumpur consultation arrangement","url":"https://www.thepaper.cn/newsDetail_forward_34565816"},{"date":"2026-11-26","impact":"A second extension of the same bond with less cash up front: the property credit chain is still repricing","src":"Economic Digest and Businesstimes via Longbridge","tag":"Property","title":"Bloomberg: Vanke is asking holders of the CNY 1.2B yuan bond due 15 Dec (the 22 Vanke MTN004 that goes to an 8 Dec vote) to defer principal by three years with the 3% coupon paid on time and an early cash repayment below half the 40% paid in January's one-year extension, with wider holder briefings from 27 Nov; nine-month net loss CNY 8.99B, contract sales −48.3%, the 2029 dollar bond at 43.3 cents; Zhuhai Huafa has repaid the two trust products it missed","url":"https://longbridge.com/zh-CN/news/306871717"},{"date":"2026-11-26","impact":"Metals bounced from an 11-month low on a quiet day; the iron-ore curve is still pointing down","src":"Sing Tao metals wire; 21st Century Business Herald; Eastmoney (Zhongxin Jingwei); Westmetall; Guoyuan Futures via Sohu","tag":"Markets","title":"Overseas 26 Nov: US markets closed for Thanksgiving (13:00 ET close on 27 Nov), US index futures +0.6% to +0.8% in the European afternoon; LME copper +1.72% to $11,850, zinc +3.54%, nickel +3.9%, aluminium +2.05%, tin +2.71% (Westmetall 25 Nov settlement $11,703, stocks 336,750 t); Brent and WTI +1% or more with OPEC+ expected to extend output targets into Q1 2027; spot gold −0.4% to $3,574.32; bitcoin above $60,000; Dalian iron ore −2.27% in the night session","url":"https://m.stnn.cc/detail/6b08a9108f9d2b19dde01754.html"}],"headline":"The State Council executive meeting published a midday readout on 27 Nov telling the 'national team' to step up market stabilisation, optimising Central Huijin's quasi-stabilisation-fund role and promising sufficient liquidity, and the CSI 300 rose 4.17% to 4,063.06, back above the October low, on three-exchange turnover of CNY 2,017.3B (+CNY 691.3B) with 5,382 stocks up against 181 down and 426 limit-ups; the Shanghai Composite rose 3.73% to 3,606.49, the ChiNext 11.61%, the STAR 50 15.07%, the Hang Seng 2.11% to 22,694.77 and the tech index 6.45%, the CSRC pledged incremental policies the same evening, the 10-year CGB closed at 1.584% (−0.9 bp), the yuan 56 pips stronger at 6.6544 with the fix at 6.7075, LME copper rose 3.29% to $12,262 after a 6.4% intraday gain and US stocks rose 1.2% to 2.3% in the half session with the Nasdaq up 6.7% on the week; Vanke's Jan-Sep sales fell 48.2% as it seeks a three-year deferral on the bond due 15 Dec; the regime stays Slowdown, the posture Risk-off with the first reversal condition met, and the PBoC stance Easing.","marketClose":"Fri 27 Nov 2026 (mainland and Hong Kong)","notes":["Mainland closes are for Friday 27 Nov: the CSI 300 (4,063.06, +162.51, +4.17%), Shanghai Composite (3,606.49, +129.61, +3.73%), Shenzhen Component (10,814.02, +7.24%), ChiNext (2,443.96, +11.61%) and STAR 50 (1,346.25, +15.07%) are the FX168 flash, matching the 21st Century Business Herald, the Sina close report and the Sina hourly reports; the CSI 300 and Shanghai open, high and low are Tencent's daily klines (sh000300 3,909.08 / 4,067.01 / 3,883.80, read after the close; sh000001 3,482.38 / 3,610.72 / 3,467.41). The STAR composite (+14.21%) and STAR 100 (+13.53%) are Time Weekly via Sohu; the BSE 50 is given as +13.20% by one Sina hourly item and 'more than 11%' by the Sina close report, so it is shown as 'about 13%'. CSI 500, CSI 1000 and SSE 50 closes were not found.","Turnover for 27 Nov is the three-exchange CNY 2,017.3B (+CNY 691.3B) from the 21st Century Business Herald and the Sina hourly reports (also printed as CNY 2.02T, +CNY 691.4B); the two-exchange figure is CNY 1,999.8B (+CNY 682.5B) per Jianying Caiguan via Sina. Breadth is 5,382 up and 181 down (Sina hourly reports; 5,380 and 'more than 5,300' elsewhere) with 426 limit-ups (21st Century Business Herald, Securities Times via Sina; 439 and 417 in other counts) and no limit-downs. Main-fund net inflow is CNY 104.874B (Tencent News) to CNY 107.7B (Sina hourly report); the 21st Century Business Herald prints a market-wide net inflow of CNY 116.387B on a different measure. Sector percentages (semiconductors +15.29%, electronic chemicals +14.74%, software +11.46%) are Eastmoney industry indexes via Tencent News and Longbridge; the Shenwan sector flows (electronics CNY 73.599B) are Time Weekly via Sohu. No margin balance for 27 Nov was found; no national-team or Central Huijin purchase amount was disclosed.","Hong Kong closes for 27 Nov are the FX168 flash (Hang Seng 22,694.77, +467.89, +2.11%; tech index 3,637.88; HSCEI 7,644.18; red chips 3,761.25), matching Sina, the 21st Century Business Herald and China News Service; the open, high, low and the HK$257.14B main-board turnover are Tencent's hkHSI daily kline (read after the close), with the turnover matching China News Service. Short selling and the full-day southbound total were not found: the 'more than HK$4B' net buy is the Securities Times item of 15:19 via Sohu, the active-stock amounts are the Zhitong morning list via Longbridge (printed in yuan-denominated 亿元 on that page and shown here as HK$), and a Futu headline putting the day at HK$4.6B was not opened. The Cailianshe page for the day's southbound total could not be read.","The State Council readout is the Xinhua text as reproduced by the 21st Century Business Herald, Time Weekly via Sohu, the Sina hourly reports and Zhitong via Longbridge; the 'first use of national team' claim is Time Weekly and Zhitong citing Tao Chuan (Guolian Minsheng) and Tian Lihui (Nankai). The CSRC statement is Securities Times and Shanghai Securities News via the 21st Century Business Herald (28 Nov 08:14 and 08:46). The PBoC Financial Stability Report, CD rules and rate-rule Q&A are the 21st Century Business Herald morning news of 28 Nov. Analyst quotes are from the 21st Century Business Herald (Chen Guo, Guo Lei, Zhao Yurui, Dong Zhongyun, Yu Fenghui), the Sina close report (Yan Xiang, Yang Delong) and the Sina hourly report (Zhang Xiaoning of JPMorgan). Background figures (ETF subscriptions above CNY 800B, buybacks CNY 315.2B, swap facility CNY 105B, re-loan quota CNY 440B, bank contracts about CNY 630B) are Cailianshe, the 21st Century Business Herald and Time Weekly citing earlier disclosures, not 27 Nov data.","The 10-year CGB point for 27 Nov is 1.584% (−0.9 bp) for the active bond 260016 at 16:30 in the 24TopNews bond daily, which also gives the 30-year 2600006 (2.04%, −1 bp), the 10-year CDB 260205 (1.718%, −1.2 bp), the futures settlements, the FR and FDR fixings, Shibor and the NCD levels; its text dates the CNY 794B operation to 20 Nov in one place, treated as a typo because China News Service and 10jqka date it 27 Nov. The −0.9 bp is against CITIC's 1.593% late print of 26 Nov; against the CFETS 1.59% it is −0.6 bp. The Sina international finance roundup of 28 Nov prints the ChinaBond 10-year curve at 1.600% and DR001 1.2823% (+0.9 bp), DR007 1.3799% (+1.4 bp) and R007 1.4234% under a '26 Nov' label that matches the 27 Nov Shibor moves, so the DR figures are shown rounded (1.28%, 1.38%) with the FDR fixings as the primary 27 Nov source. The CFETS interbank daily for 27 Nov was not found; the 21st Century Business Herald bond item and the Caijing flash could not be opened.","USD/CNY for 27 Nov is the FX168 16:30 onshore close of 6.6544 (+56 pips; the Sina roundup prints the same level as 'down 56 bp', the same move in the opposite convention), the Sing Tao 03:00 night close of 6.6541 (+68 pips, turnover $49.649B) and the Sing Tao offshore late New York level of 6.6553 (+46 pips); the fix (6.7075, +21 pips) is China News Service and FX168. The dollar index (104.03, +0.24%) and the US Treasury closes (10-year 4.928%, 5-year 4.746%, 30-year 5.325%) are the Sina roundup of 28 Nov.","Copper: Westmetall's table could not be opened at this refresh (client error), so the last settlement on file is $11,703 for 25 Nov; the 27 Nov point is the Sing Tao evening close of $12,262 (+3.29%, week +0.84%), with Wallstreetcn via 163 and Longbridge giving the 3-month contract at $12,251 (+3.2%) and the intraday high of +6.4% (Cailianshe via Sing Tao: $12,595.10 at 13:42 Beijing); the 26 Nov point ($11,850) is the same press-quote basis. Both will be replaced by the Westmetall cash settlements when the table is reachable. The Sina roundup prints LME copper at $12,262 (+3.48%), the same level with the change computed from the 26 Nov press quote. Iron ore is the Trading Economics quote for 27 Nov ($90.69, +0.06%, page updated 28 Nov); the page carries no 26 Nov print, so the prior is the 25 Nov $90.64.","US closes for the 27 Nov half session (Dow 50,774.94, S&P 500 7,297.49, Nasdaq 24,129.50) and the weekly moves are the Sina roundup and the 21st Century Business Herald morning news; the semiconductor index is 'almost 5%' with no level; oil, gold and silver levels are the Sina roundup (spot gold $3,665.02) and Wallstreetcn (COMEX gold $3,639.60, silver $43.167). The Sina US hourly report of 28 Nov 09:00 and the 21st Century Business Herald US close item could not be opened, so China ADR moves are not given. Vanke's figures are the Caixin Global digest of 27 Nov (partly paywalled).","No Chinese activity, price, credit or trade data printed on 21 to 27 Nov except October industrial profits (27 Nov). Those rows carry the figures and sources from earlier refreshes (NBS releases of 16 Nov, 9 Nov and 31 Oct; PBoC 13 Nov; GAC 10 Nov; LPR 20 Nov). Next: the NBS PMIs on 30 Nov, RatingDog manufacturing on 1 Dec. October consumer confidence is still unpublished."],"posture":{"label":"Risk-off","note":"The CSI 300 rose 162.51 points or 4.17% to 4,063.06 on 27 Nov (open 3,909.08, high 4,067.01, low 3,883.80), its first close above the 23 Oct low of 3,958.14 since 19 Nov, after the State Council executive meeting chaired by Li Qiang published its readout at midday with the first explicit instruction to 'step up the market-stabilising role of the national team', to optimise Central Huijin's quasi-stabilisation-fund function and to 'provide sufficient liquidity support': the Shanghai Composite rose 3.73% to 3,606.49 (open 3,482.38, high 3,610.72, low 3,467.41), the Shenzhen Component 7.24% to 10,814.02, the ChiNext 11.61% to 2,443.96 (its largest gain since 8 Oct 2024 and third-largest ever), the STAR 50 15.07% to 1,346.25, the STAR composite 14.21% and the BSE 50 about 13%. Three-exchange turnover jumped CNY 691.3B to CNY 2,017.3B (two exchanges CNY 1,999.8B, +CNY 682.5B), the fifth-largest single-day increase on record and the first CNY 2T session in 16 days, with 5,382 stocks up against 181 down, 426 limit-ups (the most since 8 Oct 2024) and none limit-down; semiconductors rose 15.29%, electronic chemicals 14.74% and software 11.46% while banks, coal and the high-dividend names (Shenhua, Sinopec, China Mobile) fell, main funds were a net CNY 104.9B to 107.7B in with electronics taking CNY 73.6B, and the E Fund ChiNext ETF (CNY 22.09B), Huaxia STAR 50 ETF (CNY 18.63B) and China-Korea semiconductor ETF (more than CNY 31.7B, a record) led volume. Hong Kong followed: the Hang Seng rose 467.89 points or 2.11% to 22,694.77 (open and low 22,263.70, high 22,781.03) on HK$257.14B, the tech index 6.45% to 3,637.88 with Hua Hong +20.69%, SMIC +16.39%, Zhipu +18.57%, MiniMax +17.19% and Meituan +8.21% after Q3 revenue +21.6%, the HSCEI 2.01% to 7,644.18 and red chips 1.23% to 3,761.25, with southbound investors net buyers of more than HK$4B at 15:19 after the HK$21.35B sale of 26 Nov; the week was +1.27% for the Hang Seng and +3.61% for the tech index. The CSRC's Wu Qing convened the Party committee the same day and committed to 'promptly study and issue incremental policies'. The bond market did not move (10-year CGB 1.584%, −0.9 bp) and the index is still 3.7% below the 4,217.68 reversal line after one session, so the posture stays Risk-off with the first condition now met: a second close above 3,958.14 with advancers outnumbering decliners moves the posture to Neutral, and a close above 4,217.68 on turnover near CNY 2T reverses it. The 30 Nov PMIs and the margin-ratio cut on the same day are the first test of the follow-through."},"regime":{"label":"Slowdown","note":"No activity data printed on 27 or 28 Nov, so the regime still rests on the 16 Nov release: industrial production 4.8% y/y, retail sales 0.4% with autos −21.4%, fixed-asset investment −8.1% year to date with property −21.6%, infrastructure −5.1% and manufacturing −2.9%, unemployment 5.1% and the 70-city price fall narrowing to −2.4%, with October industrial profits (27 Nov) +20.1% y/y on electronics, nonferrous, coal and chemicals while autos (−26.0%), non-metallic minerals (−46.7%), steel (−14.2%) and power (−18.4%) fell. The leading set is below 50 (NBS manufacturing PMI 49.3, new orders 49.4, non-manufacturing 49.7, construction 48.0) and consumer confidence is 89.0, so leading and coincident data agree on Slowdown. It is not Contraction because Q3 GDP is 4.5%, October exports are +35.2%, the RatingDog manufacturing PMI is 52.0 and profits are growing at 20% on prices and chips. The 27 Nov equity rally was a State Council mandate, not data; the November NBS PMIs on 30 Nov are the next test, with new orders back above 50 the condition for reopening Recovery."},"schema":1,"sections":[{"id":"leading","rows":[{"change":"−0.8","hist":[{"l":"Nov 25","v":49.2},{"l":"Dec 25","v":50.1},{"l":"Jan 26","v":49.3},{"l":"Feb 26","v":49},{"l":"Mar 26","v":50.4},{"l":"Apr 26","v":50.3},{"l":"May 26","v":50},{"l":"Jun 26","v":50.3},{"l":"Jul 26","v":49.2},{"l":"Aug 26","v":49.8},{"l":"Sep 26","v":50.1},{"l":"Oct 26","v":49.3}],"latest":"49.3","name":"NBS Manufacturing PMI","next":"30 Nov","period":"Oct 2026","prior":"50.1","read":"Fell 0.8 points to 49.3 against a 49.9 consensus, the third contraction reading in four months. Production fell 1.9 to 49.8 and new orders 1.1 to 49.4; new export orders were 48.7. Large firms held 50.2 while medium (48.4) and small (47.5) firms fell more than a point, high-tech (51.3) and equipment (50.6) stayed above 50 and consumer goods fell 1.9 to 48.8. Purchase prices fell 4.0 to 56.8 and output prices 2.3 to 51.7, still above 50 on oil; the NBS cites orders pulled forward before the holiday. The private RatingDog survey printed 52.0 two days later, so the gap between exporters and the domestic economy is 2.7 points.","ref":50,"refLabel":"50 = expansion line","signal":"warn","signalWord":"Contraction, 48-50 band","src":"NBS release (31 Oct) via The Paper, China News Service and JKN; Bloomberg consensus via China-Global South Project","trend":"down","trendWord":"Back below 50","url":"https://www.thepaper.cn/newsDetail_forward_34375155"},{"change":"−1.1","hist":[{"l":"Nov 25","v":49.2},{"l":"Dec 25","v":50.8},{"l":"Jan 26","v":49.2},{"l":"Feb 26","v":48.6},{"l":"Mar 26","v":51.6},{"l":"Apr 26","v":50.6},{"l":"May 26","v":49.9},{"l":"Jun 26","v":51.2},{"l":"Jul 26","v":48.5},{"l":"Aug 26","v":50.6},{"l":"Sep 26","v":50.5},{"l":"Oct 26","v":49.4}],"latest":"49.4","name":"NBS Manufacturing New Orders","next":"30 Nov","period":"Oct 2026","prior":"50.5","read":"The critical demand signal fell 1.1 points to 49.4, below 50 for the first time since July (48.5). The NBS says part of October demand was released before the National Day holiday, which is consistent with the September reading of 50.5 being a subsidy and pre-holiday month. Orders (49.4) are now below production (49.8), so the inventory build of September has stopped; rail, ship, aerospace and electronics kept orders at or above 53 while textiles, non-metallic minerals and non-ferrous smelting were below 50 on both.","ref":50,"refLabel":"50 = expansion line","signal":"warn","signalWord":"First sub-50 since July","src":"NBS release (31 Oct) via The Paper and China News Service (statistician Huo Lihui)","trend":"down","trendWord":"Slipped below 50","url":"https://www.chinanews.com.cn/cj/2026/10-31/10723787.shtml"},{"change":"−0.1","hist":[{"l":"Nov 25","v":49.9},{"l":"Dec 25","v":50.1},{"l":"Jan 26","v":50.3},{"l":"Feb 26","v":52.1},{"l":"Mar 26","v":50.8},{"l":"Apr 26","v":52.2},{"l":"May 26","v":51.8},{"l":"Jun 26","v":51.7},{"l":"Jul 26","v":50.9},{"l":"Aug 26","v":51.5},{"l":"Sep 26","v":52.1},{"l":"Oct 26","v":52}],"latest":"52.0","name":"RatingDog (ex-Caixin) Manufacturing PMI","next":"1 Dec","period":"Oct 2026","prior":"52.1","read":"Printed 52.0 on 2 Nov against a 51.6 Reuters consensus, little changed from September's 52.1 and an 11th straight month above 50, the longest run since mid-2021. Output grew at the fastest pace since April led by investment goods, new orders rose for a 17th month and new export orders for a fourth, though export growth slowed to a three-month low; output prices fell for the second time in three months, export prices fell for the first time in nearly a year and business confidence dropped to a nine-month low. The companion services PMI of 4 Nov fell to 50.8 from 51.6, a three-month low with selling prices down a second month and input costs rising at the fastest pace in five months, so the composite output index fell to 52.0 from 52.4. The survey of about 650 mostly export-oriented firms is 2.7 points above the official 49.3, the widest gap this year, so exporters are still growing while the domestic survey contracts.","ref":50,"refLabel":"50 = expansion line","signal":"good","signalWord":"11th month above 50","src":"S&P Global / RatingDog manufacturing release (2 Nov) and services release (4 Nov) via investinglive; Reuters consensus via investinglive","trend":"flat","trendWord":"Holding above 52","url":"https://www.pmi.spglobal.com/Public/Home/PressRelease/048ae0dea1f64839944545370ea523b4"},{"change":"−0.5","hist":[{"l":"Nov 25","v":49.5},{"l":"Dec 25","v":50.2},{"l":"Jan 26","v":49.4},{"l":"Feb 26","v":49.5},{"l":"Mar 26","v":50.1},{"l":"Apr 26","v":49.4},{"l":"May 26","v":50.1},{"l":"Jun 26","v":50.2},{"l":"Jul 26","v":49},{"l":"Aug 26","v":49},{"l":"Sep 26","v":50.2},{"l":"Oct 26","v":49.7}],"latest":"49.7","name":"NBS Non-Manufacturing PMI","next":"30 Nov","period":"Oct 2026","prior":"50.2","read":"Fell 0.5 points to 49.7 after one month above 50. Services held 50.0 (−0.2) with rail, accommodation and culture rising and finance the only major category falling notably; water transport, post and internet software stayed above 55. Construction fell 2.3 to 48.0 and its new-orders index 5.7 to 40.0, the weakest part of the survey, with construction employment at 42.0 and expectations down 3.1 to 52.3. Non-manufacturing new orders were 44.4 (−2.1) and sales prices 49.5, so services firms are still cutting prices; the private RatingDog services PMI of 4 Nov agrees, at 50.8 with selling prices falling a second month.","ref":50,"refLabel":"50 = expansion line","signal":"warn","signalWord":"Construction 48.0","src":"NBS release (31 Oct) via The Paper and Xinhua; RatingDog services PMI (4 Nov) via investinglive","trend":"down","trendWord":"Back below 50","url":"https://english.news.cn/20261031/77e098a3990746ad830789748f0e712e/c.html"},{"change":"−0.5","hist":[{"l":"Oct 25","v":89.4},{"l":"Nov 25","v":90.3},{"l":"Dec 25","v":89.5},{"l":"Jan 26","v":90.6},{"l":"Feb 26","v":91.6},{"l":"Mar 26","v":90},{"l":"Apr 26","v":89},{"l":"May 26","v":89.9},{"l":"Jun 26","v":89.4},{"l":"Jul 26","v":89.2},{"l":"Aug 26","v":89.5},{"l":"Sep 26","v":89}],"latest":"89.0","name":"Consumer Confidence Index","next":"October not yet published","period":"Sep 2026","prior":"89.5","read":"Fell 0.5 points to 89.0 in September, giving back the August uptick and more than 10 points under the neutral line; the index has been inside the 89 to 92 band since 2022 and the record low was 85.5 in November 2022. The direction is down again, from 91.6 in February, and October retail sales at 0.4% y/y with autos −21.4% say the mood is reaching spending. The NBS also reported median disposable income growth of 3.9% for January to September, slower than the 4.5% mean.","ref":100,"refLabel":"100 = neutral line","signal":"bad","signalWord":"Far below 100","src":"NBS via Dongfang Jincheng (21st Century Business Herald, 16 Nov) and TrendForce (Q3 89.0, updated 31 Oct)","trend":"down","trendWord":"Slipping again","url":"https://m.21jingji.com/article/20261116/herald/f32e9c05cac3398f9ea00907b7e4bfb2.html"},{"change":"+0.4 pt","hist":[{"l":"Dec 25","v":-2.7},{"l":"Jan 26","v":-3.1},{"l":"Feb 26","v":-3.2},{"l":"Mar 26","v":-3.4},{"l":"Apr 26","v":-3.5},{"l":"May 26","v":-3.5},{"l":"Jun 26","v":-3.3},{"l":"Jul 26","v":-3.2},{"l":"Aug 26","v":-3},{"l":"Sep 26","v":-2.8},{"l":"Oct 26","v":-2.4}],"latest":"−2.4%","name":"New Home Prices, 70 cities, y/y","next":"Mid-Dec","period":"Oct 2026","prior":"−2.8%","read":"The Reuters calculation on the NBS data has new-home prices down 2.4% y/y in October after −2.8%, the smallest fall since November 2025, and down 0.1% m/m for a fourth month at the same pace. Shanghai rose 2.7% y/y and was the only major city rising on both bases; Beijing fell 2.6%, Guangzhou 0.4% and Shenzhen 0.2%, with tier-one resale prices up an eighth month. Volumes are the other half: January to October new-home sales fell 13.7% by area and 14.3% by value, second-hand transactions rose 11.4%, and property investment fell 21.6%, so the price line is improving while the cycle that drives local-government revenue and commodity demand is still shrinking.","ref":0,"refLabel":"0 = flat prices","signal":"warn","signalWord":"40th monthly fall","src":"NBS (16 Nov) via Reuters on Investing.com and Trading Economics; NBS national economy release (sales, investment)","trend":"up","trendWord":"Decline narrowing","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/economic-indicators/drop-in-chinas-new-home-prices-narrows-to-11month-low-5028306"}],"sub":"Forward-looking. Read these first.","title":"Leading indicators"},{"id":"coincident","rows":[{"change":"−0.7 pt","hist":[{"l":"Oct 25","v":4.9},{"l":"Nov 25","v":4.8},{"l":"Dec 25","v":5.2},{"l":"Feb 26","v":6.3},{"l":"Mar 26","v":5.7},{"l":"Apr 26","v":4.1},{"l":"May 26","v":4.5},{"l":"Jun 26","v":5.3},{"l":"Jul 26","v":4.5},{"l":"Aug 26","v":5.2},{"l":"Sep 26","v":5.5},{"l":"Oct 26","v":4.8}],"latest":"+4.8%","name":"Industrial Production, y/y","next":"Mid-Dec","period":"Oct 2026","prior":"+5.5%","read":"Missed the 5.3% consensus and slowed 0.7 points from September; January to October is 5.3% and output rose 0.21% m/m. Manufacturing grew 5.4%, mining 0.7% and utilities 4.4%; high-tech manufacturing rose 17.6%, equipment 10.6% and computers and electronics 19.4%, while chemicals slowed to 1.3% and petroleum and coal processing fell for a sixth month on energy costs. Private firms grew 3.2% and state firms 2.1%, and export delivery value rose 18.6%, so production still tracks foreign demand. The NBS cited the Mid-Autumn holiday base and said domestic supply is strong and demand weak.","signal":"warn","signalWord":"Missed 5.3%, export-led","src":"NBS October release (16 Nov) via stats.gov.cn; People's Daily; Dongfang Jincheng via 21st Century Business Herald (consensus, sector detail)","trend":"down","trendWord":"Slowest since July","url":"https://www.stats.gov.cn/sj/zxfbhjd/202611/t20261116_1965844.html"},{"change":"−0.7 pt","hist":[{"l":"Oct 25","v":2.9},{"l":"Nov 25","v":1.3},{"l":"Dec 25","v":0.9},{"l":"Feb 26","v":2.8},{"l":"Mar 26","v":1.7},{"l":"Apr 26","v":0.2},{"l":"May 26","v":-0.6},{"l":"Jun 26","v":1},{"l":"Jul 26","v":0.6},{"l":"Aug 26","v":0.4},{"l":"Sep 26","v":1.1},{"l":"Oct 26","v":0.4}],"latest":"+0.4%","name":"Retail Sales, y/y","next":"Mid-Dec","period":"Oct 2026","prior":"+1.1%","read":"Rose 0.4% y/y against a 0.8% consensus, back to the August low, and 0.02% m/m against a ten-year October average of 0.45%; CNY 4.646T in the month and +1.0% year to date. Goods rose 0.3% and catering 0.7%; autos fell 21.4%, gold and jewellery 27.7% and apparel 2.0%, telecom equipment slowed to 6.5% from 31.1% as last year's subsidy base arrived, appliances rose 2.5% and petroleum products 4.4% on fuel prices; sales at units above designated size fell 4.9%. Services retail is +4.9% year to date against goods +0.9%. Under the framework this is the domestic economy the official PMIs describe, with the trade-in subsidies fading and CAAM domestic vehicle sales −26.6%.","signal":"bad","signalWord":"Autos −21.4%","src":"NBS October release (16 Nov) via stats.gov.cn; Dongfang Jincheng via 21st Century Business Herald (categories, consensus)","trend":"down","trendWord":"Back to the August low","url":"https://www.stats.gov.cn/sj/zxfbhjd/202611/t20261116_1965844.html"},{"change":"−0.9 pt","hist":[{"l":"Oct 25","v":-1.7},{"l":"Nov 25","v":-2.6},{"l":"Dec 25","v":-3.8},{"l":"Feb 26","v":1.8},{"l":"Mar 26","v":1.7},{"l":"Apr 26","v":-1.6},{"l":"May 26","v":-4.1},{"l":"Jun 26","v":-5.7},{"l":"Jul 26","v":-6.7},{"l":"Aug 26","v":-7.2},{"l":"Sep 26","v":-7.2},{"l":"Oct 26","v":-8.1}],"latest":"−8.1%","name":"Fixed Asset Investment, YTD y/y","next":"Mid-Dec","period":"Jan-Oct 2026","prior":"−7.2%","read":"Fell 8.1% y/y in January to October (CNY 36.48T) against a −6.9% to −7.0% consensus, deepening again after two months at −7.2%; October fell 2.93% m/m. Property development investment fell 21.6% (−20.6% through September), infrastructure 5.1% (−4.2%) and manufacturing 2.9% (−2.1%, autos −7.9%); private investment fell 11.4% and investment excluding property 5.1%, while intellectual-property products rose 9.2% and high-tech industry 4.0%. By sector primary fell 6.1%, secondary 3.6% and tertiary 10.9%. The September fiscal measures have not reached physical work; Dongfang Jincheng expects the infrastructure drag to narrow by year-end but property to deepen to about −22%.","ref":0,"refLabel":"0 = flat investment","signal":"bad","signalWord":"Property −21.6%, infrastructure −5.1%","src":"NBS October release (16 Nov) via stats.gov.cn; Dongfang Jincheng via 21st Century Business Herald (prior splits); EconoTimes (consensus)","trend":"down","trendWord":"Deepening again","url":"https://www.stats.gov.cn/sj/zxfbhjd/202611/t20261116_1965844.html"},{"change":"−1.1 pt","hist":[{"l":"Oct 25","v":-1.1},{"l":"Nov 25","v":5.9},{"l":"Dec 25","v":6.6},{"l":"Feb 26","v":21.8},{"l":"Mar 26","v":2.5},{"l":"Apr 26","v":14.1},{"l":"May 26","v":19.4},{"l":"Jun 26","v":27},{"l":"Jul 26","v":23.9},{"l":"Aug 26","v":25},{"l":"Sep 26","v":36.3},{"l":"Oct 26","v":35.2}],"latest":"+35.2%","name":"Exports, y/y","next":"8 Dec","period":"Oct 2026","prior":"+36.3%","read":"Exports were $412.33B in October, up 35.2% y/y against a 33.5% consensus and 36.3% in September, helped by a low base (October 2025 was −1.2%); imports rose 41.6% to $307.05B against a 32% consensus, the fastest since May 2021, so the surplus narrowed to about $105.3B from $133.53B (consensus about $125.8B) and the January to October surplus is about $1.04T. Shipments to ASEAN rose 46.3%, to the EU 24.4% and to the US 32.9% with the US surplus about $33B; integrated-circuit exports were $39.594B (+137.1%), autos $19.692B (+37.6%), phones $17.569B (+13.2%) and rare earths 4,386.0 t after 4,269.8 t, while imports of integrated circuits rose 65.1%, copper ore 28.4% and crude 4.5% in value. The exporter side of the economy is still growing at a pace the official PMIs do not show, and the import jump is chips and commodity prices more than domestic demand; November trade is due 8 Dec.","signal":"good","signalWord":"Beat, imports +41.6%","src":"GAC via Trading Economics (exports, imports, US, EU and ASEAN), investinglive and AFP via the Jakarta Post (consensus, surplus), Sina Finance (Wang Qing, Zhang Di), Jiemian via Sina (chips, autos, phones, rare earths by value), FX168 (rare-earth tonnage), Zhitong via Investing.com (yuan terms)","trend":"down","trendWord":"Slightly slower, still 35%","url":"https://tradingeconomics.com/china/exports-yoy"},{"change":"−0.1 pt","hist":[{"l":"Oct 25","v":5.1},{"l":"Nov 25","v":5.1},{"l":"Dec 25","v":5.1},{"l":"Feb 26","v":5.3},{"l":"Mar 26","v":5.4},{"l":"Apr 26","v":5.2},{"l":"May 26","v":5.1},{"l":"Jun 26","v":5},{"l":"Jul 26","v":5.2},{"l":"Aug 26","v":5.3},{"l":"Sep 26","v":5.2},{"l":"Oct 26","v":5.1}],"latest":"5.1%","name":"Surveyed Urban Unemployment","next":"Mid-Dec","period":"Oct 2026","prior":"5.2%","read":"Fell 0.1 point to 5.1%, matching October 2025, with the January to October average at 5.2%; the 31-city rate was 5.1%, local-registration workers 5.2%, migrants 4.9% (rural registration 4.8%) and the working week 48.3 hours. The September youth rate (16 to 24, ex-students) was 18%. Both PMI employment indexes are still below 50, so the rate is seasonal rather than a demand signal; it sits at the low end of the 5.0% to 5.4% range of the past three years.","signal":"neutral","signalWord":"Same as a year ago","src":"NBS October release (16 Nov) via stats.gov.cn; People's Daily","trend":"down","trendWord":"Seasonal dip","url":"https://www.stats.gov.cn/sj/zxfbhjd/202611/t20261116_1965844.html"},{"change":"+0.2 pt","hist":[{"l":"Q4 23","v":5.2},{"l":"Q1 24","v":5.3},{"l":"Q2 24","v":4.7},{"l":"Q3 24","v":4.6},{"l":"Q4 24","v":5.4},{"l":"Q1 25","v":5.4},{"l":"Q2 25","v":5.2},{"l":"Q3 25","v":4.8},{"l":"Q4 25","v":4.5},{"l":"Q1 26","v":5},{"l":"Q2 26","v":4.3},{"l":"Q3 26","v":4.5}],"latest":"+4.5%","name":"Real GDP, y/y","next":"Mid-Jan","period":"Q3 2026","prior":"+4.3%","read":"Beat the 4.4% Reuters consensus with 1.2% q/q (0.9% in Q2, consensus 1.1%), taking January to September to 4.6% and nominal GDP to CNY 107.1T; the secondary sector grew 3.8% year to date and services 5.2%. Growth is at the bottom of the 4.5% to 5.0% target range and rests on exports (September +29.6% in yuan terms) and high-tech output, with the NBS calling domestic demand \"insufficient\"; Capital Economics says the September data show the economy \"regained momentum\" while ANZ says fiscal support remains crucial. Q4 GDP is due in mid-January; a Q4 print at 4.4% or better delivers the year.","ref":5,"refLabel":"5% = top of 4.5-5% target","signal":"good","signalWord":"Bottom of target range","src":"NBS press release (19 Oct) via stats.gov.cn; investinglive; Business Recorder (Reuters)","trend":"up","trendWord":"Re-accelerating","url":"https://www.stats.gov.cn/english/PressRelease/202610/t20261019_1965619.html"}],"sub":"Confirmation of what the leading set signalled.","title":"Coincident indicators"},{"id":"policy","rows":[{"change":"−0.2 pt","hist":[{"l":"Nov 25","v":0.7},{"l":"Dec 25","v":0.8},{"l":"Jan 26","v":0.2},{"l":"Feb 26","v":1.3},{"l":"Mar 26","v":1},{"l":"Apr 26","v":1.2},{"l":"May 26","v":1.2},{"l":"Jun 26","v":1},{"l":"Jul 26","v":0.5},{"l":"Aug 26","v":0.8},{"l":"Sep 26","v":0.9},{"l":"Oct 26","v":0.7}],"latest":"+0.7%","name":"CPI, y/y","next":"9 Dec","period":"Oct 2026","prior":"+0.9%","read":"Below the 0.8% consensus and flat m/m after +0.2% in September. Food fell 2.9% y/y with the decline widening 1.2 pt (pork −8.6%, fresh vegetables −16.9%, fresh fruit −3.8%, eggs +12.3%, beef +8.7%) and fell 1.0% m/m; non-food rose 1.5%, services 0.7% (−0.1 pt), consumer goods 0.8%, energy 9.9% after 7.3% with gasoline up 22.4% y/y (+0.63 pt), and storage devices, tablets, computers and phones added about 0.26 pt; industrial consumer goods ex-energy slowed to 1.2% from 1.6%. The NBS release does not give core CPI on the pages opened (September was 1.0%). The headline is oil pushing one way and food the other, with the January to October average at 0.9%; November CPI is due 9 Dec.","ref":0,"refLabel":"0 = deflation line","signal":"warn","signalWord":"Food −2.9%, below 1%","src":"NBS release (9 Nov) via Xinhua on Sina, CGTN and People's Daily; 21st Century Business Herald (components, analysts); investinglive (consensus)","trend":"down","trendWord":"Three-month low","url":"https://news.sina.com.cn/c/2026-11-09/doc-iniyazea3009558.shtml"},{"change":"+0.7 pt","hist":[{"l":"Nov 25","v":-2.2},{"l":"Dec 25","v":-1.9},{"l":"Jan 26","v":-1.4},{"l":"Feb 26","v":-0.9},{"l":"Mar 26","v":0.5},{"l":"Apr 26","v":2.8},{"l":"May 26","v":3.9},{"l":"Jun 26","v":4.1},{"l":"Jul 26","v":3.5},{"l":"Aug 26","v":3.8},{"l":"Sep 26","v":5},{"l":"Oct 26","v":5.7}],"latest":"+5.7%","name":"PPI, y/y","next":"9 Dec","period":"Oct 2026","prior":"+5.0%","read":"Above the 5.2% to 5.3% consensus and the fastest since mid-2022, but the m/m rise slowed to 0.7% from 1.2%. Oil and gas extraction rose 6.0% m/m, refined petroleum 6.8%, organic chemicals 6.8%, coal mining 2.7%, coal processing 3.2% and gas supply 1.5%, and those six sectors gave about 0.61 pt, more than 80% of the monthly rise; by sector coal mining is +36.6% y/y, oil and gas extraction +35.0%, fuel processing +29.9%, chemicals +16.4%, gas supply +7.9% and computer and electronic equipment +5.9%, and auto prices were flat m/m after three falls. Industrial input prices rose 7.9% y/y and 1.1% m/m; the January to October PPI is +2.7%. Analysts quoted by the 21st Century Business Herald say the gain is upstream profit recovery rather than chain-wide improvement, and CICC's Zhang Di says the PPI support to growth has peaked; with Brent at $92.57 on 9 Nov against October's highs above $100, the November cost-push is smaller. October profits on 27 Nov show whether downstream losses narrow.","ref":0,"refLabel":"0 = deflation line","signal":"good","signalWord":"Cost-push, margins squeezed","src":"NBS release (9 Nov) via CGTN and People's Daily; 21st Century Business Herald (sector detail, analysts); investinglive (consensus); Sina Finance (Zhang Di); Capp Notes (Brent)","trend":"up","trendWord":"Fastest since 2022, m/m slowing","url":"https://www.21jingji.com/article/20261109/herald/4b33606f08ee0a2dd4f51c5c52f037e5.html"},{"change":"−10 bp (May 2025)","hist":[{"l":"Dec 25","v":3},{"l":"Jan 26","v":3},{"l":"Feb 26","v":3},{"l":"Mar 26","v":3},{"l":"Apr 26","v":3},{"l":"May 26","v":3},{"l":"Jun 26","v":3},{"l":"Jul 26","v":3},{"l":"Aug 26","v":3},{"l":"Sep 26","v":3},{"l":"Oct 26","v":3},{"l":"20 Nov","v":3}],"latest":"3.00%","name":"1-Year Loan Prime Rate","next":"21 Dec","period":"Since 20 May 2025","prior":"3.10%","read":"Held at 3.00% on 20 Nov for an 18th month, with the 5-year at 3.50%; the last change was the 10 bp cut of May 2025. Wang Qing of Dongfang Jincheng says bank net interest margins near historic lows give quoting banks no incentive to lower their spreads, reads the October miss as a normal monthly fluctuation with Q4 momentum still up, and expects a broad 10 to 20 bp cut in 2027 rather than soon; Dong Ximiao of Zhaolian says a small LPR fall is possible after the December Central Economic Work Conference. The PBoC eases through the instrument instead: the overnight reverse repo at 1.25% has been the main policy rate since 2 Nov, the buyback relending rate is 1.00%, new corporate loans priced at about 2.9% in October (−0.2 pt y/y) and new mortgages at about 3.1%, and the Q3 report pushes DR001-linked loan pricing. The next fixing is 21 Dec.","signal":"neutral","signalWord":"18 months unchanged","src":"PBoC LPR announcement (20 Nov) via The Paper and China News Service; 21st Century Business Herald and Jiemian via Sohu (20 Nov: Wang Qing, Dong Ximiao, loan rates); Bank of China LPR table","trend":"flat","trendWord":"Held 20 Nov","url":"https://www.chinanews.com.cn/cj/2026/11-20/10735037.shtml"},{"change":"0 bp","hist":[],"latest":"1.40%","name":"7-Day Reverse Repo Rate","period":"27 Nov 2026","prior":"1.40%","read":"The 7-day rate is 1.40% and the overnight reverse repo at 1.25% has been the main policy rate since 2 Nov. After the 25 Nov month-end package (CNY 617B overnight, CNY 500B 7-day, CNY 800B MLF against CNY 1T maturing, a CNY 321B net injection) and the CNY 45.5B net drain of 26 Nov, the PBoC lent CNY 794B overnight at 1.25% on 27 Nov against CNY 571.5B maturing, a CNY 222.5B net injection for the last session of November; the medium-term tools net a CNY 500B drain this month after the second CNY 200B MLF cut and the CNY 300B outright-repo reduction. Funding edged up on 27 Nov: FDR001 1.28% (+1.0 bp), FDR007 1.3745% (+1.45 bp), FR007 1.43% (+1.0 bp), overnight Shibor 1.28% (+0.7 bp), 7-day Shibor 1.377% (+1.0 bp), 14-day 1.3998%, 1-month 1.39%; 1-year bank NCDs about 1.41% to 1.42% in primary. The State Council's 'sufficient liquidity support' and the PBoC's Financial Stability Report line on liquidity arrangements for non-banks point at the capital-market tools, not the policy rate. The price is unchanged and the overnight tool is carrying the turn, which is what an Easing stance on hold looks like.","signal":"neutral","signalWord":"DR001 1.28%, MLF cut CNY 200B","src":"24TopNews bond daily (27 Nov: CNY 794B overnight at 1.25%, CNY 571.5B maturing, net CNY 222.5B; FDR and FR fixings; Shibor; NCD levels; CGB and CDB closes; futures); 10jqka bond midday (27 Nov: rate and maturing amount); China News Service (27 Nov operation); Sina international finance roundup of 28 Nov (DR001 1.2823%, DR007 1.3799%, R007 1.4234%); 21st Century Business Herald morning news (28 Nov: PBoC Financial Stability Report 2026)","trend":"flat","trendWord":"Overnight 1.25% anchor; CNY 222.5B net injected on 27 Nov","url":"https://24topnews.com/news/market/china-bond-market-recovers-late-session-30y-yield-dips-1bp-to-2-04-f1486ff6"},{"change":"+0.1 pt","hist":[{"l":"Nov 25","v":8.5},{"l":"Dec 25","v":8.3},{"l":"Jan 26","v":8.2},{"l":"Feb 26","v":8.2},{"l":"Mar 26","v":7.9},{"l":"Apr 26","v":7.8},{"l":"May 26","v":7.7},{"l":"Jun 26","v":7.4},{"l":"Jul 26","v":7.4},{"l":"Aug 26","v":7.2},{"l":"Sep 26","v":7.1},{"l":"Oct 26","v":7.2}],"latest":"7.2%","name":"Total Social Financing, stock y/y","next":"Mid-Dec","period":"Oct 2026","prior":"7.1%","read":"TSF stock was CNY 469.16T at end-October, up 7.2% y/y after 7.1% in September, the first increase in 15 months. The October flow was CNY 1.15T against a Caixin consensus of CNY 1.28T and CNY 815B a year earlier; January to October TSF was CNY 28.61T, CNY 2.29T less than a year earlier, with government bonds CNY 11.49T, corporate bonds CNY 3.1T (+CNY 1.27T y/y) and loans to the real economy CNY 10.91T (−CNY 3.61T y/y). The pickup is bonds and the policy financing tool, not bank lending, which is why the read is a credit impulse without private demand.","signal":"good","signalWord":"First rise in 15 months, bond-led","src":"PBoC October financial statistics and TSF release (13 Nov) via Sina Finance, The Paper and 21st Century Business Herald; Dow Jones via MarketScreener (consensus); SMM","trend":"up","trendWord":"Decelerating","url":"https://finance.sina.com.cn/jjxw/2026-11-13/doc-iniyqsna8023513.shtml"},{"change":"−0.1 pt","hist":[{"l":"Nov 25","v":8},{"l":"Dec 25","v":8.5},{"l":"Jan 26","v":9},{"l":"Feb 26","v":9},{"l":"Mar 26","v":8.5},{"l":"Apr 26","v":8.6},{"l":"May 26","v":8.6},{"l":"Jun 26","v":8},{"l":"Jul 26","v":7.7},{"l":"Aug 26","v":7.5},{"l":"Sep 26","v":7.2},{"l":"Oct 26","v":7.1}],"latest":"7.1%","name":"M2, y/y","next":"Mid-Dec","period":"Oct 2026","prior":"7.2%","read":"M2 was CNY 359.06T, up 7.1% y/y after 7.2%, below the 7.2% to 7.3% consensus; M1 was CNY 116.9T, up 4.4%, and M0 rose 10.7%. New yuan loans fell CNY 100B in October (Caixin consensus +CNY 89.7B, CNY 220B a year earlier), the third contraction this year: households −CNY 430B, corporates −CNY 160B with bills −CNY 311.7B, non-banks +CNY 347B; outstanding loans grew 4.7% (4.8% in September). Deposits grew 7.7% with fiscal deposits up CNY 3.03T year to date. Money growth is slowing while government paper replaces bank credit.","signal":"warn","signalWord":"New cycle low, loans −CNY 100B","src":"PBoC October financial statistics report (13 Nov) via Sina Finance and The Paper; Dow Jones via MarketScreener (consensus); Sing Tao","trend":"down","trendWord":"Slowing","url":"https://finance.sina.com.cn/jjxw/2026-11-13/doc-iniyqsna8023513.shtml"}],"sub":"Tracker rows added when the China page was built. They are not part of our original indicator list.","title":"Inflation and policy"},{"id":"markets","rows":[{"change":"−0.9 bp on 27 Nov","hist":[{"l":"9 Nov","v":1.587},{"l":"12 Nov","v":1.5958},{"l":"13 Nov","v":1.608},{"l":"16 Nov","v":1.63},{"l":"17 Nov","v":1.591},{"l":"18 Nov","v":1.588},{"l":"19 Nov","v":1.575},{"l":"23 Nov","v":1.5825},{"l":"24 Nov","v":1.5815},{"l":"25 Nov","v":1.59},{"l":"26 Nov","v":1.59},{"l":"27 Nov","v":1.584}],"latest":"1.584%","name":"10-Year CGB Yield","period":"27 Nov (active 10-year bond close)","prior":"1.593% on 26 Nov (CITIC late print; CFETS 1.59%)","read":"The active 10-year bond 260016 closed at 1.584% at 16:30 on 27 Nov, down 0.9 bp from the 1.593% late print of 26 Nov (1.59% on the CFETS basis), after a late recovery that took the 30-year 2600006 down 1 bp to 2.04% and the 10-year CDB 260205 down 1.2 bp to 1.718%; the futures still settled lower (TL 116.850, −0.30%; T 109.915, −0.03%; TF 106.770, −0.02%; TS 102.688, flat). The 10-year did not sell on the day the CSI 300 rose 4.17% on CNY 2T of turnover, which says the equity money came from cash, margin and the ETF bid rather than from bonds, and that the State Council's 'sufficient liquidity' is read as capital-market tools at an unchanged policy rate. The PBoC injected a net CNY 222.5B overnight for the turn with FDR001 at 1.28% (+1.0 bp). The US 10-year closed at 4.928% on 27 Nov, a gap of about 334 bp, and Guangfa's 1.45% to 1.75% range with a 1.55% centre for 2027 stands. Neutral for growth: the curve prices neither reflation nor a cut, and the 30 Nov PMIs are the next input.","signal":"neutral","signalWord":"Inside 1.55% to 1.60% on a 4% equity day","src":"24TopNews bond daily (27 Nov: 260016 1.584% −0.9 bp, 2600006 2.04% −1 bp, 260205 1.718% −1.2 bp, futures settlements, fixings, Shibor); Sina international finance roundup of 28 Nov (ChinaBond 10-year curve 1.600%; US Treasury closes); CFETS interbank daily via 10jqka and Sina hourly citing CITIC fixed income (26 Nov basis)","trend":"down","trendWord":"Slightly lower","url":"https://24topnews.com/news/market/china-bond-market-recovers-late-session-30y-yield-dips-1bp-to-2-04-f1486ff6"},{"change":"+4.17% on 27 Nov","hist":[{"l":"Dec 25","v":4629.94},{"l":"Jan 26","v":4706.34},{"l":"Feb 26","v":4710.65},{"l":"Mar 26","v":4450.05},{"l":"Apr 26","v":4807.31},{"l":"May 26","v":4892.12},{"l":"Jun 26","v":4979.43},{"l":"Jul 26","v":4588.2},{"l":"Aug 26","v":4625.09},{"l":"Sep 26","v":4357.62},{"l":"Oct 26","v":3985.5},{"l":"27 Nov","v":4063.06}],"latest":"4,063.06","name":"CSI 300","period":"27 Nov close","prior":"3,900.55 on 26 Nov","read":"The CSI 300 closed at 4,063.06 on 27 Nov, up 162.51 points or 4.17% (open 3,909.08, high 4,067.01, low 3,883.80), its first close above the 23 Oct low of 3,958.14 since 19 Nov and 3.7% below the 4,217.68 reversal line, after the State Council readout at midday told the national team to step up market stabilisation and promised sufficient liquidity. The Shanghai Composite rose 3.73% to 3,606.49 (open 3,482.38, high 3,610.72, low 3,467.41), the Shenzhen Component 7.24% to 10,814.02, the ChiNext 11.61% to 2,443.96 (largest since 8 Oct 2024), the STAR 50 15.07% to 1,346.25, the STAR composite 14.21% and the BSE 50 about 13%. Three-exchange turnover was CNY 2,017.3B, up CNY 691.3B, the fifth-largest daily increase on record and the first CNY 2T day after 15 below; 5,382 stocks rose against 181 down with 426 limit-ups (the most since 8 Oct 2024) and none limit-down; semiconductors rose 15.29%, electronic chemicals 14.74% and software 11.46%, brokers and insurers rose, banks, coal and the high-dividend names fell; main funds were a net CNY 104.9B to 107.7B in, electronics CNY 73.6B; the E Fund ChiNext ETF traded CNY 22.09B, the Huaxia STAR 50 ETF CNY 18.63B and the China-Korea semiconductor ETF a record CNY 31.7B. Chen Guo (Eastmoney Securities) reads 'national team plus sufficient liquidity' as a strong policy floor, Yu Fenghui calls it an oversold, sentiment-driven repair, JPMorgan's Zhang Xiaoning sees 4,800 next year. Signal warn: one close above the October low on CNY 2T of turnover and 30-to-1 breadth meets the first reversal condition; a second close above 3,958.14 with positive breadth moves the posture to Neutral and 4,217.68 reverses it, with the 30 Nov PMIs and the margin-ratio cut the first test.","signal":"warn","signalWord":"Above the October low, 3.7% below the reversal line","src":"FX168 flash (27 Nov: nine index closes, points and percentages); Tencent sh000300 and sh000001 daily klines (27 Nov open, high, low, close); 21st Century Business Herald (27 Nov: turnover CNY 2,017.3B and the record ranking, limit-ups, breadth, ETF volumes, sector flows, analysts); Sina stock hourly reports of 27 Nov (turnover, breadth, main-fund inflow, ETF volumes, State Council readout); Tencent News (27 Nov: sector percentages, main funds); Sina close report (27 Nov: limit-up names, ETF subscriptions)","trend":"up","trendWord":"Biggest day since October 2024","url":"https://www.fx168news.com/express/fastnews/1476363"},{"change":"+2.11% on 27 Nov","hist":[{"l":"Dec 25","v":25630.54},{"l":"Jan 26","v":27387.11},{"l":"Feb 26","v":26630.54},{"l":"Mar 26","v":24788.14},{"l":"Apr 26","v":25776.53},{"l":"May 26","v":25182.39},{"l":"Jun 26","v":22881.02},{"l":"Jul 26","v":25884.43},{"l":"Aug 26","v":25566.99},{"l":"Sep 26","v":24613.27},{"l":"Oct 26","v":23294.42},{"l":"27 Nov","v":22694.77}],"latest":"22,694.77","name":"Hang Seng","period":"27 Nov close","prior":"22,226.88 on 26 Nov","read":"The Hang Seng opened at 22,263.70 on 27 Nov, which was also the low, reached 22,781.03 and closed 467.89 points or 2.11% higher at 22,694.77 on HK$257.14B of main-board turnover, its second rise after seven falls, with the tech index up 6.45% at 3,637.88, the HSCEI up 2.01% at 7,644.18 and red chips 1.23% at 3,761.25; the week was +1.27%, +3.61% and +1.19%. Chips and AI led after the State Council readout and the US semiconductor rally: Hua Hong +20.69%, SMIC +16.39%, Biren +25.4%, Iluvatar +26.3%, GigaDevice +15.13%, Montage +14.82%, Zhipu +18.57%, MiniMax +17.19%, SenseTime +9.05%, Lenovo +8.99%; Meituan rose 8.21% after Q3 revenue +21.6% to CNY 115.56B, Alibaba 7.03%, Kuaishou 6.83%, JD 5.36%, Baidu 4.77%, Xiaomi 4.51%, Tencent 3.23%; Lingbao Gold +10%. Southbound investors were net buyers of more than HK$4B at 15:19 after the HK$21.35B index-ETF sale of 26 Nov, with Shenhua, Alibaba, SMIC (Shenzhen Connect), CCB and Meituan bought and SMIC and Tencent sold through Shanghai Connect in the morning; the full-day total was not confirmed. ICBC Asia's Ye Zeheng puts the index back inside its falling channel near the 10-day line around 22,700, with December rebalancing next; Evergrande Auto is delisted on 14 Dec and the tech index widens to 50 stocks on 7 Dec. Signal warn: a 2.11% rise that recovers the 19 Nov level (22,841.62) to within 0.6% on turnover of HK$257B, led by the AI names that fell hardest, with the mainland bid returning; short selling was not confirmed.","signal":"warn","signalWord":"Tech index +6.45%, week +1.27%","src":"FX168 flash (27 Nov: Hang Seng 22,694.77, +467.89, +2.11%; tech index, HSCEI, red chips); Tencent hkHSI daily kline (27 Nov open, high, low, close, turnover HK$257.14B); China News Service via Sohu (27 Nov: weekly moves, Meituan Q3, platform moves, Ye Zeheng); 21st Century Business Herald and Sina (27 Nov: chip and AI moves); Securities Times via Sohu (27 Nov 15:19 southbound net buy); Zhitong via Longbridge (27 Nov morning active list)","trend":"up","trendWord":"Second day up","url":"https://www.fx168news.com/express/fastnews/1476398"},{"change":"+3.73% on 27 Nov","hist":[{"l":"Dec 25","v":3968.84},{"l":"Jan 26","v":4117.95},{"l":"Feb 26","v":4162.88},{"l":"Mar 26","v":3891.86},{"l":"Apr 26","v":4112.16},{"l":"May 26","v":4068.57},{"l":"Jun 26","v":4094.4},{"l":"Jul 26","v":3832.26},{"l":"Aug 26","v":3986.3},{"l":"Sep 26","v":3842.19},{"l":"Oct 26","v":3599.02},{"l":"27 Nov","v":3606.49}],"latest":"3,606.49","name":"Shanghai Composite","period":"27 Nov close","prior":"3,476.88 on 26 Nov","read":"The Shanghai Composite opened at 3,482.38 on 27 Nov, dipped to 3,467.41 in the morning, surged after the midday State Council readout to 3,610.72 and closed at 3,606.49, up 129.61 points or 3.73%, its first close above 3,600 since 19 Nov and the largest gain of the year; the week was +2.06%. Semiconductors, communications equipment, software, brokers and insurers led, Innolight and Eoptolink traded CNY 33.4B and CNY 26.9B, while banks (Chongqing Rural Commercial, Nanjing Bank, Bank of Communications), coal and the high-dividend names fell; 426 stocks closed limit-up across the three exchanges with 5,382 up and 181 down. The index is about 15% below the mid-May high of 4,258.86, with 3,467.41 the new intraday floor and 3,455.04 (26 Nov) below it, and Hengchuang's 3,350 to 3,400 support further down. Signal warn: 3,600 recovered on CNY 2T of turnover in one session; follow-through on 30 Nov decides whether it holds.","signal":"warn","signalWord":"5,382 risers, 426 limit-ups","src":"Tencent sh000001 daily kline (27 Nov: open 3,482.38, high 3,610.72, low 3,467.41, close 3,606.49); FX168 flash (27 Nov: +129.61, +3.73%); 21st Century Business Herald and Sina hourly reports (27 Nov: sectors, breadth, weekly move, most-traded names)","trend":"up","trendWord":"Back above 3,600","url":"https://web.ifzq.gtimg.cn/appstock/app/fqkline/get?param=sh000001,day,,,5,qfq"},{"change":"−0.08% on 27 Nov","hist":[{"l":"Dec 25","v":6.9876},{"l":"Jan 26","v":6.952},{"l":"Feb 26","v":6.861},{"l":"Mar 26","v":6.8933},{"l":"Apr 26","v":6.8266},{"l":"May 26","v":6.7662},{"l":"Jun 26","v":6.7854},{"l":"Jul 26","v":6.7528},{"l":"Aug 26","v":6.7202},{"l":"Sep 26","v":6.7045},{"l":"Oct 26","v":6.6557},{"l":"27 Nov","v":6.6544}],"latest":"6.6544","name":"USD/CNY","period":"27 Nov","prior":"6.6600 on 26 Nov","read":"The onshore yuan closed at 6.6544 per dollar at 16:30 on 27 Nov, 56 pips stronger and the strongest close since 2 Nov, after a fix set 21 pips stronger at 6.7075; the night session closed at 6.6541 at 03:00 (68 pips stronger than the 6.6609 of the previous night, turnover $49.6B) and the offshore rate was 6.6553 in late New York trading, 46 pips stronger, while the dollar index rose 0.24% to 104.03 and the US 10-year closed at 4.928%. The spot rate has held between 6.6541 and 6.6736 for eleven sessions with the fix between 6.7075 and 6.7120, still about 530 pips weaker than spot, so the PBoC is leaning against appreciation rather than defending the currency; the 4.17% equity day and the State Council readout did not move it. 7.0 and 7.3 are not in play. Neutral: a firmer yuan against a stronger dollar on a risk-on day is consistent with the inflow story, not new evidence of it.","signal":"neutral","signalWord":"Range 6.65 to 6.70","src":"FX168 flash (27 Nov: onshore 16:30 close 6.6544, +56 pips); Sing Tao (28 Nov: 03:00 night close 6.6541, +68 pips, turnover; offshore late New York 6.6553, +46 pips); China News Service and FX168 (27 Nov fix 6.7075, +21 pips); Sina international finance roundup of 28 Nov (dollar index 104.03, US Treasury closes)","trend":"down","trendWord":"Yuan firmer","url":"https://www.fx168news.com/express/fastnews/1476409"},{"change":"+3.29% on 27 Nov","hist":[{"l":"Dec 25","v":12504},{"l":"Jan 26","v":13369.5},{"l":"Feb 26","v":13439.5},{"l":"Mar 26","v":12160},{"l":"Apr 26","v":13015.5},{"l":"May 26","v":13615},{"l":"Jun 26","v":13341},{"l":"Jul 26","v":13834},{"l":"Aug 26","v":14535},{"l":"Sep 26","v":14487},{"l":"Oct 26","v":14449},{"l":"27 Nov","v":12262}],"latest":"$12,262","name":"Copper, LME","period":"27 Nov LME close (press quote)","prior":"$11,850 on 26 Nov (press quote)","read":"LME copper closed 3.29% higher at $12,262 a tonne on 27 Nov (Sing Tao; Wallstreetcn puts the 3-month contract at $12,251, +3.2%) after rising as much as 6.4% to $12,595 intraday, the largest intraday gain since February, and ended three weekly falls with a 0.84% weekly gain; the Shanghai main contract rose 5.5% (7.1% intraday) and COMEX December copper 3.38% to $5.517 a pound, the largest daily gain since 8 Apr. Saxo's Ole Hansen credits the Chinese stabilisation signal and the AI-stock recovery, ING's Ewa Manthey and Warren Patterson short covering, and Mysteel AI demand expectations; the 25 Nov intraday low of $11,650 was an 11-month low. Tin rose 8.65% to $41,170, zinc 1.68% to $3,563.50, nickel 0.44% to $15,800, aluminium fell 0.77% to $2,787 and lead 0.80% to $1,856. Monitored stocks are about 1.105M t, a five-month high after rising in seven of eight weeks, and the Yangshan premium about $320 against a $500 record. Westmetall's table could not be opened at this refresh, so the 26 and 27 Nov points are press quotes on an evening-close basis and will be replaced by the cash settlements when posted; the last settlement is $11,703 for 25 Nov. At $12,262 copper is 13% below the 9 Nov settlement of $14,030 and about 15% down on the month, so the demand-gauge signal stays bad; a return above $14,000 with stocks falling would restore warn.","signal":"bad","signalWord":"13% below 9 Nov, stocks at a five-month high","src":"Sing Tao (stnn) metals wire (27 Nov: LME copper $12,262 +3.29%, tin, zinc, nickel, aluminium, lead, weekly moves); Wallstreetcn via 163 and Longbridge (27 Nov: 3-month $12,251 +3.2%, intraday +6.4%, SHFE, COMEX, stocks, Yangshan premium, Hansen); Cailianshe via Sing Tao (27 Nov intraday $12,595.10); PiQ Markets and FinScans (27 Nov: ING, Mysteel, weekly context); Trading Economics (27 Nov copper futures summary); Westmetall (last settlement 25 Nov $11,703; table not reachable at this refresh)","trend":"up","trendWord":"Biggest intraday gain since February","url":"https://m.stnn.cc/detail/6b0a0eb88f9d2b19dde90d94.html"},{"change":"+0.06% on 27 Nov","hist":[],"latest":"$90.69/t","name":"Iron Ore","period":"27 Nov","prior":"$90.64/t on 25 Nov","read":"Quoted at $90.69 a tonne for 27 Nov (62% Fe CFR Tianjin), up 0.06% on the day per Trading Economics, 0.01% lower on the month and 13.50% lower on the year; the page carries no 26 Nov print. Iron ore did not join the 27 Nov metals rally (copper +3.29%, tin +8.65%) because its demand is construction, not AI: property investment −21.6% and infrastructure −5.1% year to date, cement output −1.3%, the construction PMI at 48.0, steel-industry profits −14.2% and non-metallic mineral profits −46.7% for January to October, and Vanke's January to September sales −48.2% with a three-year deferral sought on the bond due 15 Dec. Signal bad: the price is holding $90 only because supply is being managed, and the State Council's equity measures do not reach the property chain.","signal":"bad","signalWord":"Property investment −21.6%, below $92","src":"Trading Economics (27 Nov quote, daily, monthly and yearly change; page updated 28 Nov); Caixin Global (27 Nov: Vanke sales and cash); NBS industrial profits release via Sina (27 Nov)","trend":"flat","trendWord":"Flat at $90.69","url":"https://tradingeconomics.com/commodity/iron-ore"}],"sub":"Additions to the leading and coincident core. Closes for Monday 19 Oct in the mainland, copper and iron ore; Hong Kong was closed on 19 Oct, so the Hang Seng is the 16 Oct close and 20 Oct figures in the text are midday levels.","title":"Market readings"}],"takeaways":["The State Council put the national team in writing. The executive meeting chaired by Li Qiang on 27 Nov issued its readout at midday rather than after the close, said the capital market 'bears on the overall economic situation', and listed: keep improving the market-stabilisation mechanism, implement existing policies and plan incremental ones; push listed companies to raise dividends and buybacks; 'step up the market-stabilising role of the national team' and further optimise Central Huijin's quasi-stabilisation-fund function; 'provide sufficient liquidity support'; improve the policies guiding insurance, enterprise-annuity and social-security money into the market; strengthen defences against imported risk; accelerate the multi-tier market; and punish financial fraud and illegal share reductions. It is the second capital-market readout in a month (6 Nov was the first) and the first to name the national team (Tao Chuan of Guolian Minsheng, Tian Lihui of Nankai). The CSRC's Wu Qing convened an enlarged Party committee the same day and committed to 'implement existing policies in detail and, with relevant parties, promptly study and issue incremental policies', with the same five headings; the PBoC's Financial Stability Report 2026 says it is studying liquidity arrangements for non-banks in specific scenarios. Chen Guo of Eastmoney Securities calls 'national team plus sufficient liquidity' a strong policy floor, Guo Lei of Guangfa says institutionalised stabilisation lowers the tail-risk premium, and Yu Fenghui calls the day an oversold, sentiment-driven repair rather than a confirmed fundamental reversal; JPMorgan's Zhang Xiaoning puts the CSI 300 at 4,800 next year. Background: equity-ETF net subscriptions have exceeded CNY 800B since early October (Cailianshe), 2026 buybacks announced total CNY 315.2B to 26 Nov, the swap facility has run two batches of CNY 105B and the buyback re-loan quota about CNY 440B, the re-loan rate was cut to 1% and the big four banks signed about CNY 630B of buyback-loan contracts on 24 to 26 Nov.","The mainland had its biggest day since October 2024. The CSI 300 closed at 4,063.06 on 27 Nov, up 162.51 points or 4.17% (open 3,909.08, high 4,067.01, low 3,883.80), its first close above the 23 Oct low of 3,958.14 since 19 Nov and 3.7% below the 4,217.68 reversal line; the Shanghai Composite rose 3.73% to 3,606.49 (open 3,482.38, high 3,610.72, low 3,467.41), back above 3,600, the Shenzhen Component 7.24% to 10,814.02, the ChiNext 11.61% to 2,443.96 (the year's best day and the third-largest ever after +17.25% on 8 Oct 2024 and +15.36% on 30 Sep 2024), the STAR 50 15.07% to 1,346.25, the STAR composite 14.21%, the STAR 100 13.53% and the BSE 50 about 13%. Three-exchange turnover was CNY 2,017.3B, up CNY 691.3B (two exchanges CNY 1,999.8B, +CNY 682.5B), the fifth-largest single-day increase on record after 30 Sep 2024 (CNY 1.15T), 8 Oct 2024, 8 Apr 2024 and 18 Sep 2025, and the first session above CNY 2T after 15 below; 5,382 stocks rose against 181 down, 1,766 rose more than 9%, 426 closed limit-up (439 on the Securities Times count), the most since 8 Oct 2024, and none limit-down. Semiconductors rose 15.29%, electronic chemicals 14.74%, software 11.46%, with more than 550 chip stocks up 10% or at the limit: Hua Hong, NAURA, AMEC, GigaDevice, Piotech, ACM Shanghai, Hwatsing and Cambricon at or near 20%, Innolight (CNY 33.4B traded), Eoptolink (CNY 26.9B, limit-up) and CXMT (CNY 18.6B) up more than 10%, Unitree and the humanoid names at 20%; Xiangcai and Guosheng Securities limit-up, Eastmoney and Hualin +8%, New China Life +5.13%; banks (Chongqing Rural Commercial, Nanjing Bank, Bank of Communications), coal and the high-dividend names (Shenhua, Sinopec, China Mobile) fell. Main funds were a net CNY 104.9B (Tencent) to CNY 107.7B (Sina) in, electronics CNY 73.6B, computing CNY 23.7B, communications CNY 20.2B and machinery CNY 15.6B; the E Fund ChiNext ETF traded CNY 22.09B, the Huaxia STAR 50 ETF CNY 18.63B, the Southern CSI 1000 ETF CNY 13.82B, the Huatai-PineBridge CSI 300 ETF CNY 12.37B and the China-Korea semiconductor ETF more than CNY 31.7B, a record, with the STAR chip ETFs at the 20% limit and the Bosera bank ETF −1.97%. On the week the Shanghai Composite rose 2.06%, the Shenzhen Component 5.44% and the ChiNext 10.48%. The CSI 300 and SSE 50 sample changes take effect after the 11 Dec close (30 CSI 300 names), and the Shenzhen indexes on 14 Dec.","Hong Kong rose with the mainland and the AI trade. The Hang Seng opened at 22,263.70, its low, reached 22,781.03 and closed 467.89 points or 2.11% higher at 22,694.77 on HK$257.14B of main-board turnover, the tech index rose 6.45% to 3,637.88, the HSCEI 2.01% to 7,644.18 and red chips 1.23% to 3,761.25; the week was +1.27%, +3.61% and +1.19%. Chips and AI led: Hua Hong +20.69%, SMIC +16.39%, Biren +25.4%, Iluvatar +26.3%, GigaDevice +15.13%, Montage +14.82%, Innoscience +12.61%, Zhipu +18.57%, MiniMax +17.19% (its chief executive said it will speed adoption of Huawei and Alibaba chips), SenseTime +9.05%, Lenovo +8.99%; the platforms followed Meituan, which rose 8.21% after Q3 revenue of CNY 115.56B (+21.6%) and adjusted net profit of CNY 1.85B, with Alibaba +7.03%, Kuaishou +6.83%, JD +5.36%, Baidu +4.77%, Xiaomi +4.51%, NetEase +3.84% and Tencent +3.23%; Lingbao Gold rose more than 10% as gold rebounded. Southbound investors were net buyers of more than HK$4B at 15:19 (Securities Times) after the HK$21.35B sale of 26 Nov; the morning's active list had Shanghai Connect buying Shenhua (HK$1.11B) and Alibaba (HK$856M) and selling SMIC (HK$389M) and Tencent (HK$326M), with Shenzhen Connect buying SMIC (HK$900M), CCB (HK$414M), Alibaba (HK$411M) and Meituan (HK$342M); the full-day total and split were not confirmed. ICBC Asia's Ye Zeheng notes the index is back inside its falling trend channel and near the 10-day line around 22,700, with December fund rebalancing the next factor. The Listing Committee cancelled Evergrande Auto's listing (last trading 11 Dec, delisting 14 Dec); the tech index widening to 50 stocks takes effect on 7 Dec. The Nikkei rose 2.11% to 58,711.11 and the Kospi 4.34% to 4,915.68 with SK Hynix +6.14% and Samsung +4.55%.","The bond market stayed still and the yuan firmed into the turn. The PBoC lent CNY 794B overnight at 1.25% on 27 Nov against CNY 571.5B maturing, a CNY 222.5B net injection, and funding edged up: FDR001 1.28% (+1.0 bp), FDR007 1.3745% (+1.45 bp), FR001 1.40% (−1.0 bp), FR007 1.43% (+1.0 bp), overnight Shibor 1.28% (+0.7 bp), 7-day 1.377% (+1.0 bp), 14-day 1.3998%, 1-month 1.39%; 3-month state and joint-stock bank NCDs printed about 1.35% to 1.36% and 1-year about 1.41% to 1.42% in primary, with the secondary 1-year at about 1.4275% (+0.75 bp). The active 10-year CGB 260016 closed at 1.584% at 16:30, down 0.9 bp, the 30-year 2600006 at 2.04% (−1 bp) and the 10-year CDB 260205 at 1.718% (−1.2 bp) after a late recovery, while the futures settled lower: TL 116.850 (−0.30%), T 109.915 (−0.03%), TF 106.770 (−0.02%), TS 102.688 (flat); exchange-traded property bonds were volatile (20 Huafa −20%, 24 Huazong 01 −16%, 25 Zhuhua Y3 +34%). A 4% equity day that leaves the 10-year inside 1.55% to 1.60% says the money went from cash and leverage to stocks, not from bonds. The fix was 6.7075 (+21 pips) and the onshore yuan closed 56 pips stronger at 6.6544 at 16:30, with the 03:00 night close at 6.6541 (+68 pips, turnover $49.6B) and the offshore rate at 6.6553 in late New York (+46 pips); the dollar index rose 0.24% to 104.03 and the US 10-year closed at 4.928% with the 5-year at 4.746% and the 30-year at 5.325%, so the gap to the CGB is about 334 bp. The PBoC also issued the large-denomination CD rules (effective 21 Mar 2027; CNY 100,000 minimum for individuals, CNY 5M for institutions) and the revised deposit and loan rate rules that drop the penalty-rate range.","Copper had its best day since February, US stocks rose into the weekend and Vanke's numbers got worse. LME copper closed 3.29% higher at $12,262 (Sing Tao; the 3-month at $12,251, +3.2%, per Wallstreetcn) after rising 6.4% intraday to $12,595, the largest intraday gain since February, ending three weekly falls at +0.84% on the week; the Shanghai main contract rose 5.5% (7.1% intraday) and COMEX December copper 3.38% to $5.517 a pound, the largest daily gain since 8 Apr, with Saxo's Ole Hansen citing the Chinese stabilisation signal and the AI-stock recovery and ING's Ewa Manthey and Warren Patterson short covering; monitored stocks are about 1.105M t, a five-month high, and the Yangshan premium about $320. Tin rose 8.65% to $41,170, zinc 1.68% to $3,563.50, nickel 0.44% to $15,800, aluminium fell 0.77% to $2,787 and lead 0.80% to $1,856; iron ore rose 0.06% to $90.69 (Trading Economics, 27 Nov). In the US half session the Dow rose 1.18% to 50,774.94 (+5.5% on the week), the S&P 500 1.60% to 7,297.49 (+5.6%) and the Nasdaq 2.31% to 24,129.50 (+6.7%), the Philadelphia semiconductor index almost 5% (+9% on the week) with SanDisk +16%, Micron and SK Hynix +7%, Coherent +14% and Lumentum +8%; COMEX gold rose 2.94% to $3,639.60 (spot $3,665.02 late) and silver 7.76% to $43.167, WTI fell 0.72% to $83.08 and Brent 1.17% to $95.44; the DAX rose 2.14% to 25,231.42. Caixin reports Vanke's January to September contract sales fell 48.2% to CNY 52B with operating cash outflow of CNY 2.2B and cash of CNY 52.5B at end-September (−CNY 6.6B from June), that it proposes a three-year deferral on the CNY 1.2B 22 Vanke MTN004 due 15 Dec with an upfront cash payment 'well below' the 40% of the first extension, that the underwriters were to brief holders on 27 Nov ahead of the 8 Dec vote, and that it intends bond-by-bond talks rather than a comprehensive restructuring. The markets score rises from 22 to 30 and the composite from 42 to 44; growth 40, inflation 48 and policy 60 are unchanged, because nothing printed for the real economy and the State Council measures are equity liquidity, not demand."],"translation":[{"body":"The CSI 300 closed at 4,063.06 on 27 Nov, up 4.17% on three-exchange turnover of CNY 2,017.3B (+CNY 691.3B, the fifth-largest daily increase on record) with 5,382 stocks up against 181 down and 426 limit-ups, after the State Council told the national team to step up stabilisation and promised sufficient liquidity at midday; the ChiNext rose 11.61% and the STAR 50 15.07% with semiconductors +15.29%, and the Hang Seng rose 2.11% to 22,694.77 with the tech index +6.45%. Under the framework this is a policy floor being written into the institutions (national team named, Central Huijin's quasi-stabilisation-fund role, CSRC incremental policies, the 30 Nov margin cut) rather than a data turn: the leading set is still below 50, the 16 Nov coincident data missed and the profit growth is upstream and chips. The index now sits above the 3,958.14 October low with the first reversal condition met and 4,217.68 as the line that changes the posture; the pattern to compare is 30 Sep and 8 Oct 2024, when similar days were followed by a retracement before a higher range. The leaders are the AI-hardware, chip-equipment and broker names that fell hardest, the laggards are banks and the high-dividend names that had been the only bid, so the rotation is from defensives into beta. The 30 Nov PMIs decide whether the readings that drove the November sell-off (new orders 49.4, retail sales 0.4%) are joined by any improvement; without it the rally is liquidity.","title":"Equities"},{"body":"The active 10-year CGB closed at 1.584% on 27 Nov (−0.9 bp), the 30-year at 2.04% and the 10-year CDB at 1.718%, with the futures slightly lower, on the day the CSI 300 rose 4.17%: the bond market did not fund the equity rally and does not read 'sufficient liquidity' as a policy-rate move. The curve stays inside 1.55% to 1.60% with the PBoC's overnight tool at 1.25% injecting a net CNY 222.5B for the turn, FDR001 at 1.28% and 1-year NCDs about 1.42%, and the US 10-year at 4.928% leaves a gap of about 334 bp with the Fed priced for a December hike. The yuan closed 56 pips stronger at 6.6544 with the night session at 6.6541 and the offshore rate at 6.6553 as the dollar index rose to 104.03, and the fix at 6.7075 stays about 530 pips weaker than spot, so the PBoC is still leaning against appreciation. The property credit chain is the divergence: exchange-traded Huafa and Huazong bonds fell 16% to 20% on 27 Nov and Vanke's January to September sales fell 48.2% with cash of CNY 52.5B as it seeks a three-year deferral with a small upfront payment, so the equity floor does not extend to developer credit. A 10-year below 1.55% on a weak PMI or above 1.65% on supply would be the moves to note.","title":"Fixed income and currency"},{"body":"The policy answer to the November sell-off has moved from the exchanges (22 Nov) to the State Council (27 Nov): the readout names the national team for the first time, assigns Central Huijin a quasi-stabilisation-fund function, promises sufficient liquidity, pushes dividends and buybacks, widens the channels for insurance, annuity and social-security money and adds imported-risk defences, and the CSRC committed the same evening to incremental policies while the PBoC's Financial Stability Report studies liquidity arrangements for non-banks; the mechanics already in place are the swap facility (two batches, CNY 105B), the buyback re-loan (about CNY 440B of quota at 1%, about CNY 630B of bank contracts signed this week), equity-ETF subscriptions above CNY 800B since October and the margin-ratio cut to 80% on 30 Nov. Money is carried through the overnight tool at 1.25% (CNY 794B on 27 Nov, net +CNY 222.5B) with the MLF cut by CNY 200B for a second month, so the stance is Easing by instrument with the price unchanged and the quantity trimmed; the LPR is on hold at 3.00%. Under the framework the equity support raises the markets reading and leaves growth, inflation and policy where they were, because it is leverage, flow and signalling rather than demand: the real-economy tests are the 30 Nov PMIs, the 8 Dec trade data, the 9 Dec CPI and PPI and the December Politburo meeting and Central Economic Work Conference, where a fiscal or property measure would move the regime; the external test is the Section 301 hearing on 25 Jan 2027 and the 10 Jan truce date.","title":"Liquidity and policy"}]};
